{"id": "8", "pred": "The key difference between tartrate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartarar acid.", "raw_output": "The key difference between tartrate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartarar acid.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between tartate and succinate is their chemical derivation: succinate is derived from succinic acid while tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Additionally, succinate is an extended-release drug that stays in the bloodstream for 24 hours, making it a once-per-day pill. On the other hand, tartrate is an immediate-release drug that does not stay in the bloodstream for 24 hours and needs to be taken at regular intervals. Another important difference is that succinate has a greater dehydrating effect and may cause side effects like constipation and dry mouth, whereas tartrate may cause diarrhea and sleep issues like insomnia or unusual dreams.", "question": "what is the difference between tartate and succinate", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 262.962, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 34, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 12183, 376, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 429, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 20038, 92335, 13621, 323, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 44815, 277, 277, 13621, 13], "logp_list": [-0.1903, -0.2451, -0.0313, -0.0063, -0.5507, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0018, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.006, -0.0051, -0.002, -0.0129, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.057, -0.0063, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.0551, -0.009, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0628, -0.0114, -0.4831, -0.0087, -0.0022, -0.0242], "cumulative_logprob": -1.778, "norm_logp": -0.0523, "input_len": 525, "output_tokens": 34, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "22", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. The", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. The", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure the delivery of quality behavioral health services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and work towards improving the overall health and well-being of Virginians. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and host weekly Q&A sessions for providers to address their questions and issues.", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 186.455, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 26, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 18432, 264, 17059, 1618, 1817, 6602, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 481, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 576], "logp_list": [-0.1184, -0.0005, -0.0853, -0.0002, -2.4595, -0.2441, -0.002, -0.0353, -0.0432, -0.0002, -0.0127, -0.0007, -0.0006, -0.0439, -0.0014, -0.0283, -0.1315, -0.0014, -0.0003, -0.0037, -0.1351, -0.2217, -0.0046, -0.0003, -0.0239, -0.424], "cumulative_logprob": -4.0228, "norm_logp": -0.1547, "input_len": 319, "output_tokens": 26, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "28", "pred": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry on the jamb until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from it's original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "raw_output": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry on the jamb until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from it's original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps based on the given passages:\n1. Close the door and attempt to lock it.\n2. If it doesn't lock, open the door and use a chisel to tap and pry off the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Remove the top door stop as well.\n3. Place the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it 1/4 inch from its original location using the distinct line left behind.\n4. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n5. If the latch still doesn't catch, tighten the hinges first.\n6. Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb if necessary.\n7. Enlarge the strike plate hole or move the strike plate if the latch doesn't align with it.\n8. Ensure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\nFollowing these steps should help fix the door lock issue.", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 1739.703, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 2, "n_tokens": 139, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 432, 594, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13], "logp_list": [-2.1908, -0.0041, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.0078, -0.0058, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0216, -0.0461, -0.0049, -0.0107, -0.0706, -0.0023, -0.2896, -0.03, -0.0062, -0.0001, -0.4524, -0.0453, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0064, -0.0441, -0.0152, -0.0043, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0033, -0.0016, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0416, -0.0055, -0.7497, -0.1196, -1.1651, -0.0003, -0.2099, -0.1528, -0.0153, -0.0024, -0.1529, -0.0148, -0.0908, -0.0162, -0.01, -0.0271, -0.033, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0022, -0.0006, -0.0073, -0.0026, -0.0104, -0.0792, -0.0519, -0.0003, -0.6003, -0.2231, -0.0114, -0.0039, -0.0234, -0.0044, -0.0074, -0.0339, -0.0019, -0.0008, -0.0233, -0.009, -0.0085, -0.0019, -0.0277, -0.0029, -0.0022, -0.0023, -0.0045, -0.0016, -0.7059, -0.0107, -0.0018, -0.0048, -0.0049, -0.2475, -0.0085, -0.0022, -0.0004, -0.0227, -0.0002, -0.0021, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.0038, -0.0029, -0.071, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0059, -0.0017, -0.0085, -0.0038, -0.0028, -0.0016, -0.0363, -0.0095, -0.0026, -0.0009, -0.0005, -0.004, -0.0071, -0.0042, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0059, -0.0007, -0.008, -0.0039, -0.0004, -0.0016, -0.007, -0.1019, -0.0004, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0034, -0.0014, -0.0004, -0.0108, -0.0323], "cumulative_logprob": -8.5939, "norm_logp": -0.0618, "input_len": 511, "output_tokens": 139, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.02, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "33", "pred": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees f (175 degrees c). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off", "raw_output": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees f (175 degrees c). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off", "gt": "To cook pollock, first preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper and place them on the baking sheet. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes. If desired, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet and return fish to the oven to allow cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 450.216, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 53, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 282, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 272, 568, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 13, 52074, 304, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 11999, 23387, 1007], "logp_list": [-0.9853, -0.0022, -0.3049, -0.0235, -0.0138, -0.2225, -0.0016, -0.0008, -0.0087, -0.1057, -0.0619, -0.002, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0089, -0.1674, -0.2041, -0.0547, -0.0035, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0006, -0.0157, -0.0284, -0.0067, -0.0075, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0114, -0.0053, -0.169, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0044, -0.0016, -0.0011, -0.0027, -0.0003, -0.0047, -0.0047, -0.1504, -0.0283, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -2.6237, "norm_logp": -0.0495, "input_len": 267, "output_tokens": 53, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "37", "pred": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees f (175 degrees c). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off", "raw_output": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees f (175 degrees c). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook pollock:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) (Passage 2).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper (Passage 1 and 2).\n3. Place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet lined with butter-flavored cooking spray (Passage 1).\n4. Add onion, green pepper, and tomato slices to the baking sheet (Passage 1).\n5. Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily (Passage 1 and 2).\n6. To add cheesy flavor, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven for an additional 3 minutes (Passage 3).\n\nNote that Passage 3 does not provide any specific instructions for cooking the pollock, but rather suggests adding cheese to the existing dish.", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 11.404, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 53, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 282, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 272, 568, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 13, 52074, 304, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 11999, 23387, 1007], "logp_list": [-0.9853, -0.0022, -0.3049, -0.0235, -0.0138, -0.2225, -0.0016, -0.0008, -0.0087, -0.1057, -0.0619, -0.002, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0089, -0.1674, -0.2041, -0.0547, -0.0035, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0006, -0.0157, -0.0284, -0.0067, -0.0075, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0114, -0.0053, -0.169, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0044, -0.0016, -0.0011, -0.0027, -0.0003, -0.0047, -0.0047, -0.1504, -0.0283, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -2.6237, "norm_logp": -0.0495, "input_len": 267, "output_tokens": 53, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "42", "pred": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "raw_output": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. (Passage 1)\n2. Heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. Once heated, use a cloth to peel off the plastic. (Passage 2)\n3. Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and use it to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element after leaving it on the element for 5 minutes. Then, wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth and remove any remaining residue with a cloth dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to remove plastic from the drum of a clothes dryer.", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 24.026, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 120, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [6727, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 304, 6291, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 13], "logp_list": [-1.648, -0.004, -0.0002, -0.0025, -0.0014, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0015, -0.0016, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0417, -0.0007, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.1027, -0.1711, -0.0, -0.006, -0.0003, -0.0033, -0.0048, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.008, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0353, -0.4267, -0.0497, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0155, -0.0001, -0.0045, -0.094, -0.0112, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0017, -0.0144, -0.0056, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.1069, -0.1356, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0519, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0038, -0.0026, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1849, -0.0032, -0.004, -0.0104, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7647, -0.0768, -0.0028, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0038, -0.0281, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.003, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0016, -0.0007, -0.0424], "cumulative_logprob": -4.1081, "norm_logp": -0.0342, "input_len": 584, "output_tokens": 120, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.72, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "47", "pred": "Step 1: Lay your quilt on a bed, table or or flat surface. Step 2: Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 3: Fold the lower left corner on toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 4: Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 5: Making sure the fold is on the bias, fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt.", "raw_output": "Step 1: Lay your quilt on a bed, table or or flat surface. Step 2: Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 3: Fold the lower left corner on toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 4: Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 5: Making sure the fold is on the bias, fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt.", "gt": "To fold a quilt, follow these steps:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface such as a bed or table.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n5. Finally, fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is also on the bias.", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 25.378, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 118, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 43924, 697, 60736, 389, 264, 4845, 11, 1965, 476, 476, 10063, 7329, 13, 14822, 220, 17, 25, 60473, 279, 4722, 1290, 9131, 705, 8841, 279, 4126, 315, 279, 60736, 3259, 2704, 279, 1155