{"id": "135", "pred": "Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.) Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil on each exposed head, using your", "raw_output": "Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.) Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil on each exposed head, using your", "gt": "Here are brief answers to the question on how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nPassage 1: The passage does not provide information on how to roast individual garlic cloves specifically. However, it does mention that larger garlic cloves may take up to an hour to soften when roasted, so it is possible to assume that smaller cloves will take less time.\n\nPassage 2: This passage provides some options for seasoning the garlic before roasting, but it does not provide instructions on how to roast individual garlic cloves.\n\nPassage 3: This passage provides a method for roasting entire garlic heads, but it does not address how to roast individual garlic cloves. The passage does mention that cutting the top of the garlic bulb and exposing the individual cloves can help them roast more evenly, but it does not provide specific instructions on how to do this.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 24.598, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 120, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 11616, 356, 568, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 264, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 320, 32, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 6138, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 389, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697], "logp_list": [-1.0049, -0.0014, -0.2591, -0.0003, -0.0042, -0.001, -0.0024, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.0258, -0.0566, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.021, -0.2858, -0.1746, -0.4182, -0.0032, -0.0023, -0.0003, -0.0028, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0049, -0.0111, -0.0075, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0113, -0.005, -0.0055, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0015, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0133, -0.0001, -0.003, -0.0411, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0007, -0.0036, -0.0023, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0019, -0.1138, -0.0014, -0.0026, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0024, -0.0109, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0016, -0.0002, -0.0084, -0.0247, -0.0015, -0.0009, -0.0133, -0.0039, -0.0003, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0052, -0.003, -0.0037, -0.0994, -0.0784, -0.7134, -0.0023, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.049, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0089, -0.0137, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0386, -0.0019, -0.0437, -0.0072, -0.0131, -0.00