{"id": "236", "pred": "The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by an annual precipitation of 34 inches, with an average of 256 sunny days per year. The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees, while the lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees. The", "raw_output": "The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by an annual precipitation of 34 inches, with an average of 256 sunny days per year. The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees, while the lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees. The", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\n\n* Temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 50°F (December) to 58°F (September).\n* Precipitation: Sausalito receives an average of 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January (0 inches).\n* Air Quality Index: The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\n* Sunshine: Sausalito experiences 256 sunny days per year, with an average of 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n* Comfort Index: According to Sperling's comfort index, Sausalito has a score of 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable year-round climate.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages regarding the average weather in Sausalito during a specific month or time period.", "question": "average weather sausalito", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.38, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 60, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 31871, 553, 458, 9775, 59950, 315, 220, 18, 19, 14924, 11, 448, 458, 5461, 315, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 13, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6122, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 11, 1393, 279, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6652, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 13, 576], "logp_list": [-0.8445, -0.1514, -0.3684, -0.07, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0001, -1.1775, -0.4311, -0.0145, -1.0855, -0.6424, -0.2925, -0.0137, -0.0087, -0.0206, -0.065, -0.0027, -0.0818, -0.4838, -1.3566, -0.1006, -0.6425, -0.0053, -0.3536, -0.1888, -0.0073, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0543, -0.0001, -0.1406, -0.1341, -0.7461, -0.2903, -0.0217, -0.0021, -0.7097, -0.2266, -0.0183, -0.022, -0.0059, -0.0038, -0.0003, -0.014, -0.1902, -0.0048, -0.0025, -0.1715, -0.0005, -0.0041, -0.3212, -0.0044, -0.0126, -0.0003, -0.0057, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.6645], "cumulative_logprob": -12.1849, "norm_logp": -0.2031, "input_len": 429, "output_tokens": 60, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "244", "pred": "The difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like", "raw_output": "The difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like", "gt": "The FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) have several differences. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Another important difference is the requirement of disability. The ADA requires a physical or mental impairment to substantially limit a major life activity, while the FEHA only requires that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without the need for it to be a substantial limit.", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 9.031, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 45, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 279, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 19853, 279, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 11, 323, 432, 3171, 1405, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 1075], "logp_list": [-1.3182, -0.8005, -0.0169, -0.4456, -0.0004, -0.1145, -0.0574, -0.1809, -0.0329, -0.7643, -0.1017, -0.0341, -0.015, -0.2216, -0.0129, -0.0103, -0.0056, -0.0012, -0.0016, -0.0424, -0.0216, -0.0026, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0011, -0.0367, -0.0292, -0.0144, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0148, -0.0015, -0.0011, -0.038, -0.0055, -0.0019, -0.0007, -0.5937, -0.0043, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0012, -0.0012, -0.0186], "cumulative_logprob": -4.9687, "norm_logp": -0.1104, "input_len": 266, "output_tokens": 45, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "249", "pred": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavor flavor until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops that indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "raw_output": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavor flavor until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops that indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, start by preheating an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow to stand for 10 minutes. Finally, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 22.333, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 109, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 