{"id": "255", "pred": "To clean your dryer vent, remove the outside cover on the vent, and use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.", "raw_output": "To clean your dryer vent, remove the outside cover on the vent, and use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.", "gt": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove the cover.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole of the vent.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n6. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning that area as well.\n7. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and remove the lint filter frame for easier access to clean.\n8. This thorough cleaning will help your dryer run efficiently and reduce the risk of house fires.\n\nNote: The information provided in the given passages is sufficient to answer the question.", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.721, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 33, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 697, 46622, 10378, 11, 4057, 279, 4889, 3421, 389, 279, 10378, 11, 323, 990, 264, 3281, 57920, 15625, 448, 458, 13036, 480, 3705, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 13647, 13], "logp_list": [-0.5767, -0.0025, -0.6985, -0.0022, -0.0011, -0.0187, -0.4791, -0.0002, -0.0071, -0.0132, -0.0084, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.1279, -0.0236, -0.0082, -0.0008, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0012, -0.0005, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0081], "cumulative_logprob": -1.9858, "norm_logp": -0.0602, "input_len": 491, "output_tokens": 33, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.49, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "260", "pred": "MSM powder benefits the body by helping to get oxygen into the blood a lot more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels, helping to absorb more nutrients (vitamins and minerals), relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "raw_output": "MSM powder benefits the body by helping to get oxygen into the blood a lot more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels, helping to absorb more nutrients (vitamins and minerals), relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "gt": "MSM powder offers several benefits. It helps get oxygen into the blood more efficiently, thereby increasing energy levels. It also makes cell walls more permeable. The powder aids in the absorption of more nutrients, particularly when paired with Co-enzyme Q10. Additionally, MSM powder can help relieve muscular aches and pains and reduce inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "question": "the benefits of msm powder", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.334, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 61, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4826, 44, 16723, 7567, 279, 2487, 553, 10476, 311, 633, 23552, 1119, 279, 6543, 264, 2696, 803, 29720, 448, 279, 1852, 3311, 315, 975, 11, 7703, 4802, 5866, 11, 10476, 311, 34306, 803, 36393, 320, 54811, 37825, 323, 32972, 701, 58544, 4405, 51092, 264, 8528, 323, 50166, 11, 323, 17719, 36040, 4152, 311, 10895, 476, 46188, 18808, 1741, 438, 54552, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3569, -0.0003, -0.3481, -0.5603, -0.1942, -0.0039, -0.3897, -0.2007, -0.0513, -0.062, -0.0154, -0.0013, -0.0017, -0.0017, -0.6034, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0536, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.3085, -0.3628, -0.0044, -0.3321, -0.5897, -0.3749, -0.915, -0.158, -0.0114, -0.0018, -0.6025, -0.0085, -0.0183, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.071, -1.002, -0.0002, -0.0041, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0033, -0.0008, -0.0162, -0.0705, -0.0026, -0.0018, -0.0317, -0.0, -0.0018, -0.0037, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.042, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0507], "cumulative_logprob": -8.8392, "norm_logp": -0.1449, "input_len": 242, "output_tokens": 61, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "266", "pred": "Introduction to Visual Merchandising: The visual merchandiser is aware of the retail strategy and the company goals of the retailer in order to project the same in the store. Earlier retailers used advertising as the only media to", "raw_output": "Introduction to Visual Merchandising: The visual merchandiser is aware of the retail strategy and the company goals of the retailer in order to project the same in the store. Earlier retailers used advertising as the only media to", "gt": "Visual merchandising is a strategy used by retailers to attract customers to their store and influence their buying behavior. It involves the presentation of the store and its merchandise in a way that aligns with the retailer's goals and marketing strategy. The visual merchandiser's role is crucial as they not only help bring customers to the store but also influence their purchasing decisions, akin to \"making the horse drink\" as per G. Surrendar's analogy. Particularly, visual merchandising related to shop windows has been found to significantly impact consumer buying behavior, with variations observed based on gender and the store attributes most valued by consumers in shopping centers.", "question": "introduction to visual merchandising and relation to the consumer", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.841, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 44, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [37155, 311, 20185, 65025, 437, 3791, 25, 576, 9124, 21733, 437, 12059, 374, 7853, 315, 279, 10806, 8282, 323, 279, 2813, 8845, 315, 279, 36791, 304, 1973, 311, 2390, 279, 1852, 304, 279, 3553, 13, 46893, 29182, 1483, 12876, 438, 279, 1172, 3687, 311], "logp_list": [-1.2335, -0.037, -0.0562, -0.0038, -0.0001, -0.0049, -0.5018, -0.1064, -0.0069, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0109, -0.0247, -0.0017, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0027, -0.0004, -0.0035, -0.0018, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0076, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0015, -0.0017, -0.0008, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0237, -0.2382, -0.0014, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0038, -0.0002], "cumulative_logprob": -2.2807, "norm_logp": -0.0518, "input_len": 253, "output_tokens": 44, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "278", "pred": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition that virtually no symptoms until severe bone damage has already occurred. Once the bones have been weakened by bone density loss, symptoms may include: 1  Back pain.2  Loss of height over time with stooped posture. 3  Fractures of the vertebrae, wrists,", "raw_output": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition that virtually no symptoms until severe bone damage has already occurred. Once the bones have been weakened by bone density loss, symptoms may include: 1  Back pain.2  Loss of height over time with stooped posture. 3  Fractures of the vertebrae, wrists,", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a condition where the bones have been significantly weakened to the point of causing symptoms such as back pain, loss of height, and fractures. According to passage 3, osteoporosis typically has no symptoms until significant bone damage has occurred, making it a \"silent disease\" until it reaches this advanced stage. Passage 2 also highlights that compression fractures of the spine are a common cause of osteoporosis pain, which can be severe and debilitating. Therefore, severe osteoporosis is characterized by a high risk of fractures, particularly in the spine and hips, as well as persistent back pain and loss of height.", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 13.755, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 67, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1514, 19289, 51268, 88666, 10704, 374, 264, 2971, 429, 21214, 902, 13495, 3080, 15386, 17240, 5557, 702, 2669, 10017, 13, 9646, 279, 24854, 614, 1012, 57664, 553, 17240, 17457, 4709, 11, 13495, 1231, 2924, 25, 220, 16, 220, 6841, 6646, 13, 17, 220, 24704, 315, 2608, 916, 882, 448, 42032, 16367, 47278, 13, 220, 18, 220, 2869, 531, 1413, 315, 279, 5198, 50213, 68, 11, 85778, 11], "logp_list": [-0.4546, -0.0003, -0.0059, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.8968, -1.1135, -0.0109, -0.8744, -0.9025, -0.1524, -0.0012, -0.0264, -0.024, -0.0027, -0.0043, -0.3608, -0.0198, -0.0009, -0.0204, -0.9922, -0.001, -0.0013, -0.0027, -0.0024, -0.0009, -0.0021, -0.0015, -0.0009, -0.0021, -0.0429, -0.0109, -0.0045, -0.0022, -0.1969, -0.2691, -0.0063, -0.6287, -0.0171, -0.0005, -0.0263, -0.1728, -0.0076, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.4116, -0.0186, -0.0009, -0.0035, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0016, -0.1337, -0.1884, -0.1076, -0.0018, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0006, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -8.1387, "norm_logp": -0.1215, "input_len": 500, "output_tokens": 67, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "286", "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.Next, cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking.When internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for  30 minutes before serving.", "raw_output": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.Next, cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking.When internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for  30 minutes before serving.", "gt": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 325-350 degrees Fahrenheit. If you don't have time to defrost the roast, put it in the oven at 250 F for about an hour. Afterwards, take it out and season it with salt, pepper, and any seasonings you prefer, such as thyme, oregano or garlic. Rub the surface with 2 tsp. of olive oil. Place the roast in a roasting pan with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards, and put it back in the oven for about 1.5 to 3 hours depending on its size, or about 20-30 minutes per pound. Make sure the roast is cooked thoroughly by using a meat thermometer; the internal temperature should reach 150 degrees Fahrenheit. Once it is cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 26.64, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 127, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1191, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10224, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 18501, 11, 4296, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 11, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 50761, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 374, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 11, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13], "logp_list": [-0.7936, -0.0121, -0.0025, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0119, -0.0258, -0.0031, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0656, -0.5686, -0.0014, -0.0133, -0.002, -0.0, -0.0197, -0.0001, -0.0153, -0.0045, -0.1179, -0.0241, -0.0002, -0.0037, -0.0285, -0.0136, -0.2243, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.006, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0028, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0088, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.9111, -0.0004, -0.0017, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0011, -0.0017, -0.0003, -0.0129, -0.0124, -0.0591, -0.0002, -0.0343, -0.0009, -0.0019, -0.0058, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0042, -0.0019, -0.1218, -0.0029, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.0909, -0.0341, -0.0028, -0.0007, -0.0007, -0.0009, -0.001, -0.0008, -0.0009, -0.0015, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0009, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0026, -0.0033, -0.0064, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.001, -0.0003, -0.0021, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.038, -0.0004, -0.0222,