{"id": "484", "pred": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked due to the use of third-party apps. Snapchat cannot guarantee your security", "raw_output": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked due to the use of third-party apps. Snapchat cannot guarantee your security", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is why your Snapchat account might be temporarily locked:\n\n1. Using third-party apps to access Snapchat without authorization: According to passage 2, Snapchat does not guarantee the security of accounts accessed through third-party apps. If you have been using such apps, it could result in your account being locked.\n2. Exceeding the limit of warnings for third-party app usage: Passage 1 mentions that Snapchat sends warnings before locking accounts that use third-party apps excessively. If you have exceeded the limit of warnings, your account might be temporarily locked.\n\nTherefore, the most likely reason for your Snapchat account being temporarily locked is due to the unauthorized use of third-party apps.", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 4.373, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 21, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [7771, 55179, 2692, 1231, 387, 27092, 16061, 4152, 311, 279, 990, 315, 4843, 24031, 10500, 13, 55179, 4157, 15440, 697, 4763], "logp_list": [-1.6514, -0.0214, -0.1446, -0.8242, -0.3304, -0.115, -0.0013, -0.6971, -0.0001, -0.2309, -0.0516, -0.0079, -0.1387, -0.0165, -0.128, -0.4931, -0.6848, -0.4079, -0.005, -0.584, -0.0593], "cumulative_logprob": -6.5932, "norm_logp": -0.314, "input_len": 496, "output_tokens": 21, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "490", "pred": "By using a website which is able to check the popular tweets which favorite as well as people who favorite your tweets.", "raw_output": "By using a website which is able to check the popular tweets which favorite as well as people who favorite your tweets.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can track who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as their favorite.", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 5.157, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 23, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1359, 1667, 264, 3910, 892, 374, 2952, 311, 1779, 279, 5411, 23150, 892, 6930, 438, 1632, 438, 1251, 879, 6930, 697, 23150, 13], "logp_list": [-1.7138, -0.5236, -0.3438, -0.1204, -0.8167, -0.5125, -0.0077, -0.0024, -0.0257, -0.5032, -0.076, -0.0088, -0.1277, -0.5861, -0.027, -0.0022, -0.0154, -0.0229, -0.1681, -0.0569, -0.1124, -0.0073, -0.1039], "cumulative_logprob": -5.8845, "norm_logp": -0.2558, "input_len": 429, "output_tokens": 23, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "495", "pred": "Salary exchange is a way of making pension contributions that could allow both employers and employees to save money. An employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in", "raw_output": "Answer: Salary exchange is a way of making pension contributions that could allow both employers and employees to save money. An employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in", "gt": "Salary exchange pension contributions, also known as salary sacrifice, is a method where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This can allow both employers and employees to save money. The salary that is waived under the salary exchange is equal to the value of the regular pension contribution made. For example, it could be 7.5% or 9% of the pay, depending on the pension scheme. The employer then pays a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme.", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.245, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 35, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 41758, 9289, 374, 264, 1616, 315, 3259, 27681, 19026, 429, 1410, 2138, 2176, 22426, 323, 8256, 311, 3581, 3220, 13, 1527, 9364, 32908, 311, 2968, 705, 949, 315, 862, 16107, 476, 12037, 304], "logp_list": [-0.8257, -0.1094, -0.2095, -0.1931, -0.5099, -0.0105, -0.1741, -0.1425, -0.0069, -0.0014, -0.0012, -0.4035, -0.0821, -0.0031, -0.0006, -0.0036, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0003, -0.0069, -0.0018, -0.0506, -1.6597, -0.0018, -0.0361, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0846, -0.029, -0.0005, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.007, -0.0008, -0.0098], "cumulative_logprob": -4.5692, "norm_logp": -0.1305, "input_len": 467, "output_tokens": 35, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-