{"id": "503", "pred": "Oily skin is hereditary", "raw_output": "Answer: Oily skin is hereditary", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main factors that contribute to oily skin are:\n\n1. Genetics: According to passage 1, oily skin is hereditary, meaning that if one's parents have oily skin, they are more likely to experience it themselves.\n2. Hormonal shifts: Passage 1 suggests that hormonal changes in the body can cause oily skin to come and go.\n3. Diet: While diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin, according to passage 1.\n4. Poor hygiene: Passage 2 mentions that poor hygiene and topical applications can contribute to oily skin.\n5. Combination skin: Passage 3 defines different skin types, including combination skin, which can be prone to oily skin in certain areas, such as the T-zone.\n\nThere is no additional information provided in the passages to suggest other factors that might contribute to oily skin. Therefore, the answer to the question is based on the information provided in the passages.", "question": "factors that cause oily skin", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 1.925, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 8, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 506, 1541, 6787, 374, 1059, 94354], "logp_list": [-1.0437, -0.0187, -0.5052, -0.0015, -0.2558, -0.1447, -0.4208, -0.0003], "cumulative_logprob": -2.3907, "norm_logp": -0.2988, "input_len": 497, "output_tokens": 8, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "509", "pred": "The difference between the two is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks and", "raw_output": "The difference between the two is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks and", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that porterhouse steak is a larger version of T-Bone steak and it contains more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steak.", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.718, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 42, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1378, 374, 429, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 5610, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 1091, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 323], "logp_list": [-0.6034, -0.1012, -0.0196, -1.0703, -0.1475, -0.0484, -0.0022, -0.0673, -0.0008, -0.0038, -0.0009, -0.0067, -0.0004, -0.0026, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0009, -0.1275, -0.0041, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0048, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0106, -0.0068, -0.0001, -0.0115, -0.0012, -0.0099, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.1018], "cumulative_logprob": -2.3663, "norm_logp": -0.0563, "input_len": 442, "output_tokens": 42, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "519", "pred": "The reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards. Your entry ticket has a number on it from 1 to approximately 55. Tickets are $50 each and a table consists of 20 individuals, which constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. and two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pull. individuals totaling twenty.", "raw_output": "The reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards. Your entry ticket has a number on it from 1 to approximately 55. Tickets are $50 each and a table consists of 20 individuals, which constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. and two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pull. individuals totaling twenty.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how raffles work:\n\n1. Reverse Raffle: In this type of raffle, the numbers on the entry tickets are drawn in reverse order, starting with the last number and ending with the first number. For example, if there are 55 entries, the last number drawn wins the grand prize, followed by the next-to-last number, and so on until the first number. Each entry ticket costs $50, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket worth $1,000 and two $500 prizes (for the early bird drawing and the first ticket pulled).\n2. 50-50 Draw: This is a raffle held during a single day at a specific event. Tickets are sold to patrons throughout the event by roving staff with handheld electronic devices. The gross proceeds of 50-50 tickets sold at the event go into a prize pool, and 50% of the prize pool is awarded to the winner of a random draw that takes place at the end of the event. The remaining 50% goes to a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n3. Additional Raffles: In addition to the main raffle, there may be additional raffles for drinks and dinner. These raffles are not included in the original ticket price and require separate entry fees. One of these raffles offers the chance to win $10,000!\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "question": "how do raffles work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 16.849, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 82, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 9931, 435, 44090, 374, 264, 435, 44090, 714, 28412, 13, 4615, 4343, 11727, 702, 264, 1372, 389, 432, 504, 220, 16, 311, 13187, 220, 20, 20, 13, 35615, 525, 400, 20, 15, 1817, 323, 264, 1965, 17167, 315, 220, 17, 15, 7775, 11, 892, 41575, 825, 4583, 11727, 518, 400, 16, 15, 15, 15, 13, 323, 1378, 400, 20, 15, 15, 37408, 320, 603, 369, 279, 4124, 11958, 13330, 323, 825, 369, 279, 1156, 11727, 6815, 13, 7775, 81123, 17073, 13], "logp_list": [-1.641, -0.514, -0.0015, -0.0005, -0.7915, -0.0226, -0.1065, -0.0014, -0.0877, -0.0056, -0.2979, -0.125, -0.0021, -0.0033, -0.017, -0.0319, -0.0003, -0.0015, -0.0003, -0.0014, -0.0016, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0117, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0126, -0.0677, -0.0045, -0.0098, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0006, -0.0145, -0.0018, -0.0006, -0.0028, -0.0008, -0.0032, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0052, -0.0188, -0.0015, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0018, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0911, -0.0262, -0.0018, -0.0095, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0114, -0.0026, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.2708, -0.0003, -0.0019, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0311, -0.162, -0.1275, -0.0079, -0.0021, -0.0506], "cumulative_logprob": -4.6185, "norm_logp": -0.0563, "input_len": 353, "output_tokens": 82, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.77, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
