{"id": "550", "pred": "A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power. It is composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current. It is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in transistors designed for high-power applications. Unlike", "raw_output": "A transistor is a semiconductor device used to amplify and switch electronic signals and electrical power. It is composed of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. The collector current is approximately β (common-emitter current gain) times the base current. It is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in transistors designed for high-power applications. Unlike", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a transistor is an electronic component made of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It functions as an amplifier or a switch depending on the flow of electrons through its base. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a small electric current at one end and produces a larger electric current at the other. The flow of electrons is controlled by using a small amount of electricity to turn a valve-like structure in the transistor. In its off state, the holes in the base act as a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector. Transistors can have common-emitter configuration where collector current is approximately β times the base current.", "question": "what is a transistor how does it work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 17.006, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 84, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32, 97941, 374, 264, 86736, 3671, 1483, 311, 96068, 323, 3398, 14346, 17289, 323, 19734, 2355, 13, 1084, 374, 23415, 315, 86736, 3684, 448, 518, 3245, 2326, 52979, 369, 3633, 311, 458, 9250, 16224, 13, 576, 31953, 1482, 374, 13187, 33218, 320, 5464, 36512, 3248, 1482, 8722, 8, 3039, 279, 2331, 1482, 13, 1084, 374, 11136, 7046, 1091, 220, 16, 15, 15, 369, 2613, 1331, 25719, 1356, 380, 1087, 714, 646, 387, 9155, 304, 1356, 380, 1087, 6188, 369, 1550, 26526, 8357, 13, 26048], "logp_list": [-0.121, -0.0024, -0.0332, -0.0456, -0.2576, -0.0035, -0.2278, -0.011, -0.0013, -0.0054, -0.001, -0.0089, -0.0006, -0.0301, -0.0005, -0.0041, -0.1611, -0.2916, -0.6024, -0.0494, -0.0001, -0.0074, -0.001, -0.0103, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0028, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1362, -0.8946, -0.3859, -0.0011, -0.0312, -0.0057, -0.0095, -0.0821, -0.002, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.4678, -0.0589, -0.0323, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0037, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0202, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0083, -0.0004, -0.001, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.107, -0.1315], "cumulative_logprob": -4.2741, "norm_logp": -0.0509, "input_len": 413, "output_tokens": 84, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.8, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "571", "pred": "LT (hold) + RB (tap)", "raw_output": "LT (hold) + RB (tap)", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to perform skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One:\n\n1. Ball Juggle (while standing): Press and hold the LT button on the Xbox controller, followed by a quick tap of the RB button.\n\nThat's it! This combination will allow you to perform the ball juggling skill move while standing on the field in FIFA 16 on Xbox One.", "question": "how to do the skill moves on fifa 16 for xbox one", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 6.842, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 9, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [27404, 320, 6282, 8, 488, 27974, 320, 30047, 8], "logp_list": [-1.1022, -0.0628, -0.004, -0.0051, -0.0093, -0.0013, -0.0134, -0.0005, -0.5337], "cumulative_logprob": -1.7323, "norm_logp": -0.1925, "input_len": 299, "output_tokens": 9, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.02, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "575", "pred": "To quickly get rid of mice, you need to take immediate action. This is a", "raw_output": "To quickly get rid of mice, you need to take immediate action. This is a", "gt": "To quickly get rid of mice, you should take immediate action by sealing off entry points that mice could use to enter your home. Steel wool is a good material to use for this purpose as it will prevent mice from using the hole to get back into your house. Additionally, getting rid of rats and mice involves eliminating any sources of food and shelter for these rodents and preventing them from returning.", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 3.544, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 17, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 6157, 633, 9279, 315, 23627, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 1896, 13922, 1917, 13, 1096, 374, 264], "logp_list": [-1.4829, -0.0525, -0.0563, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0268, -0.9429, -0.1799, -0.0017, -0.0215, -0.0013, -0.0016, -0.5001, -0.7367, -0.0734, -0.0284], "cumulative_logprob": -4.1065, "norm_logp": -0.2416, "input_len": 272, "output_tokens": 17, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 1.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "592", "pred": "Form 1099-PATR (Taxable Distributions Received From Cooperatives) should be", "raw_output": "Form 1099-PATR (Taxable Distributions Received From Cooperatives) should be", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"Where does 1099-PATR go on 1040?\" is:\n\nSchedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835.\n\nAccording to the instructions for Form 1099-PATR, patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1, 2, 3, and 5 from a cooperative are reported on one of these forms.", "question": "where does 1099-patr go on 1040", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 4.579, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 21, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1838, 220, 16, 15, 24, 24, 9299, 828, 49, 320, 31349, 480, 422, 17994, 38417, 5542, 23517, 5859, 8, 1265, 387], "logp_list": [-1.2033, -0.0134, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0001, -1.3471, -0.0038, -0.0, -0.4753, -0.008, -0.0131, -0.0087, -0.0006, -0.0027, -0.2485, -0.6887, -0.0937], "cumulative_logprob": -4.111, "norm_logp": -0.1958, "input_len": 279, "output_tokens": 21, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
