{"id": "610", "pred": "Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. Keep a master schedule for to make any changes. Microsoft Excel", "raw_output": "Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. Keep a master schedule for to make any changes. Microsoft Excel", "gt": "To create an employee schedule, start by making a list of all employees and their duties (Passage 2). Then, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day (Passage 2). Print out copies of the schedule for employees or send them via email (Passage 3). If you need to make any changes, keep a master schedule and update it as needed (Passage 3). Microsoft Excel is a useful tool for creating schedules for multiple employees and can be used as your business grows (Passage 3). It's important to note that there may be other work laws that you need to follow, such as paying overtime if you schedule an employee more than 40 hours per week (Passage 1).", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.875, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 53, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [8078, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 13, 7405, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 311, 1281, 894, 4344, 13, 5100, 21029], "logp_list": [-1.9307, -0.0039, -0.0499, -0.0042, -0.0922, -0.0254, -0.0009, -0.0052, -0.0048, -0.0001, -0.0031, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.8807, -0.1247, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.002, -0.0002, -0.0016, -0.0008, -0.0031, -0.0001, -0.0027, -0.0002, -0.0175, -0.0187, -0.6675, -0.0022, -0.0003, -0.0135, -0.001, -0.0134, -0.0019, -0.0015, -0.0013, -0.0092, -0.0012, -0.0004, -0.0041, -0.1026, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.036, -0.0148, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0091, -0.549, -0.0014], "cumulative_logprob": -4.6068, "norm_logp": -0.0869, "input_len": 248, "output_tokens": 53, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "616", "pred": "Step 2: Remove the printer from the devices list. Remove printers and uninstall any Windows print drivers using Windows Devices and Printers. If your printer connects to the computer with a USB cable, disconnect the cable from the printer. Turn the printer off and on again, and", "raw_output": "Step 2: Remove the printer from the devices list. Remove printers and uninstall any Windows print drivers using Windows Devices and Printers. If your printer connects to the computer with a USB cable, disconnect the cable from the printer. Turn the printer off and on again, and", "gt": "To force removal of a printer in devices and printers:\n1. Use Print Manager or Printers folder to remove the printer or printer port.\n2. Close Print Manager or the Printers folder.\n3. Stop and restart the Spooler Service.\n4. Go to Control Panel > Hardware and Sound > Printers.\n5. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then select Delete.\n6. If the printer is connected to the computer via USB cable, disconnect it from the printer.\n7. Turn off the printer and turn it back on again. Ensure that it is in a ready state.\n8. Remove the printer from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers.", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 11.049, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 55, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 17, 25, 10783, 279, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 13, 10783, 55953, 323, 53635, 894, 5515, 1173, 11788, 1667, 5515, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 13, 1416, 697, 22380, 33061, 311, 279, 6366, 448, 264, 11348, 14652, 11, 28969, 279, 14652, 504, 279, 22380, 13, 11999, 279, 22380, 1007, 323, 389, 1549, 11, 323], "logp_list": [-2.109, -0.0119