{"id": "648", "pred": "The color of urine can vary based on several factors, including the presence of blood, certain foods and medications, and kidney diseases. A normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this pale color of urine is sometimes altered when, in case of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunction function", "raw_output": "The color of urine can vary based on several factors, including the presence of blood, certain foods and medications, and kidney diseases. A normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this pale color of urine is sometimes altered when, in case of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunction function", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Normal urine is typically pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome. If kidney diseases are present, the filtration and re-absorption stages of urine production may be malfunctioning, altering this pale color. Red urine is typically a sign of blood in the urine, which can indicate serious conditions like infections or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Foods and medications can also affect urine color, with beets, berries, and fava beans being among the most likely to cause changes.", "question": "color of urin meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 15.415, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 77, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 3118, 389, 3807, 9363, 11, 2670, 279, 9362, 315, 6543, 11, 3654, 15298, 323, 29910, 11, 323, 37942, 18808, 13, 362, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 419, 27539, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 7025, 28752, 979, 11, 304, 1142, 315, 37942, 18808, 11, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 525, 71187, 729], "logp_list": [-0.2917, -0.0261, -0.0022, -0.0233, -0.0528, -1.0328, -1.171, -0.0004, -0.6472, -0.0018, -0.886, -0.073, -0.5647, -0.0345, -0.0019, -0.1356, -0.266, -0.4401, -0.3125, -0.5159, -0.0035, -0.0171, -0.1814, -1.1767, -0.1835, -0.0602, -1.3676, -0.61, -0.5066, -0.5314, -0.0014, -0.0081, -0.0422, -0.0002, -0.5233, -0.7909, -0.0131, -0.019, -0.0001, -0.0098, -0.0003, -0.0038, -0.0, -0.0, -0.012, -0.1881, -0.0, -1.508, -0.1634, -0.0013, -0.0238, -0.0009, -0.1701, -0.0006, -0.0016, -0.0924, -0.106, -0.0008, -0.058, -0.0006, -0.0022, -0.0007, -0.0054, -0.0072, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0024, -0.0026, -0.0083, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0011, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.1744, -0.0032, -0.5051], "cumulative_logprob": -15.5745, "norm_logp": -0.2023, "input_len": 243, "output_tokens": 77, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.86, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "652", "pred": "The color of urine can vary based on several factors, including the presence of blood, certain foods and medications, and kidney diseases. A normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this pale color of urine is sometimes altered when, in case of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunction function", "raw_output": "The color of urine can vary based on several factors, including the presence of blood, certain foods and medications, and kidney diseases. A normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this pale color of urine is sometimes altered when, in case of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunction function", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the color of urine can indicate various things. Here's what we can infer from the passages:\n\n* Red urine (passage 1) indicates the presence of blood in the urine, which can be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer.\n* Deep purple urine (passage 2) is associated with porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Certain foods and medications can also change urine color.\n* The normal color of urine is pale yellow (passage 3), but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is the meaning of different colors of urine?\" based on these passages is:\n\nRed urine can indicate the presence of blood in the urine, while deep purple urine is associated with porphyria. Changes in urine color can also be caused by kidney diseases.", "question": "color of urin meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 15.472, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 77, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 3118, 389, 3807, 9363, 11, 2670, 279, 9362, 315, 6543, 11, 3654, 15298, 323, 29910, 11, 323, 37942, 18808, 13, 362, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 419, 27539, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 7025, 28752, 979, 11, 304, 1142, 315, 37942, 18808, 11, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 525, 71187, 729], "logp_list": [-0.2917, -0.0261, -0.0022, -0.0233, -0.0528, -1.0328, -1.171, -0.0004, -0.6472, -0.0018, -0.886, -0.073, -0.5647, -0.0345, -0.0019, -0.1356, -0.266, -0.4401, -0.3125, -0.5159, -0.0035, -0.0171, -0.1814, -1.1767, -0.1835, -0.0602, -1.3676, -0.61, -0.5066, -0.5314, -0.0014, -0.0081, -0.0422, -0.0002, -0.5233, -0.7909, -0.0131, -0.019, -0.0001, -0.0098, -0.0003, -0.0038, -0.0, -0.0, -0.012, -0.1881, -0.0, -1.508, -0.1634, -0.0013, -0.0238, -0.0009, -0.1701, -0.0006, -0.0016, -0.0924, -0.106, -0.0008, -0.058, -0.0006, -0.0022, -0.0007, -0.0054, -0.0072, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0024, -0.0026, -0.0083, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0011, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.1744, -0.0032, -0.5051], "cumulative_logprob": -15.5745, "norm_logp": -0.2023, "input_len": 243, "output_tokens": 77, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "657", "pred": "Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion.", "raw_output": "Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Wet your hair thoroughly.\n3. Apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is longer.\n4. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n5. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n6. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n7. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles.\n8. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\n\nTherefore, the steps to properly clean your hair are:\n\n1. Choose the right products.\n2. Wet your hair.\n3. Shampoo your hair.\n4. Rinse and detangle.\n5. Condition your hair.\n6. Rinse and comb.\n7. Dry your hair with a towel.\n8. Use a hair dryer.", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 16.63, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 81, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [49, 258, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 323, 11, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 990, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 13, 26530, 279, 64324, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 28337, 1137, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 13], "logp_list": [-1.5496, -0.0021, -0.0001, -0.1992, -0.0003, -0.0561, -0.7533, -0.1297, -0.0266, -0.0038, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0026, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0044, -0.002, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0014, -0.001, -0.0004, -0.0571, -0.3346, -0.0083, -0.0003, -0.007, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0055, -0.2239, -0.0098, -0.0001, -0.0093, -0.0048, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0209, -0.0019, -0.0004, -0.0008, -0.0007, -0.1846, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.0051, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0022, -0.0001, -0.0049, -0.0031, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0032, -0.0156, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0081], "cumulative_logprob": -3.6646, "norm_logp": -0.0452, "input_len": 406, "output_tokens": 81, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.72, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "664", "pred": "When you inhale, the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered and air is sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "raw_output": "When you inhale, the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered and air is sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "gt": "When you breathe in, or inhale, the intercostal muscles contract and expand the ribcage while the diaphragm contracts and pulls downward to increase the volume of the chest. This lowers the pressure inside the chest and allows air to be sucked into the lungs through the windpipe. When you breathe out, or exhale, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, and the intercostal muscles also relax. This reduces the space in the chest cavity and forces out air that is rich in carbon dioxide out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 24.787, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 