{"id": "673", "pred": "The weighted average method of inventory costing assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is", "raw_output": "The weighted average method of inventory costing assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is", "gt": "Sure! Here's my answer to the question:\n\nThe weighted average method of costing inventory assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. When a unit of inventory is sold, the weighted average method takes the average cost of all inventories currently available and assigns that average price to the item sold. Since inventory prices fluctuate, the weighted average cost will also change.\n\nTo calculate the weighted average cost per unit, divide the cost of goods available for sale by the number of units available for sale. The weighted-average figure can then be used to assign costs to both ending inventory and cost of goods sold. The recorded amount of inventory on hand using the weighted average costing method represents a value between the oldest and newest units purchased into stock.\n\nWeighted average costing is commonly used in situations where inventory items are intermingled and it is impossible to assign a specific cost to an individual unit, or when the accounting system is not sophisticated enough to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers.", "question": "inventory costing weighted average", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 3.987, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 19, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 36824, 5461, 1714, 315, 15444, 53724, 49912, 458, 5461, 2783, 311, 1817, 6573, 315, 15444, 979, 432, 374], "logp_list": [-0.6447, -0.2266, -0.0088, -0.0671, -0.3579, -0.4354, -0.0046, -0.155, -0.0755, -0.0001, -0.0032, -0.0124, -0.0027, -0.0613, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0264, -0.0019, -0.0003], "cumulative_logprob": -2.0839, "norm_logp": -0.1097, "input_len": 482, "output_tokens": 19, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "681", "pred": "To get a free VoIP service and phone number, you can visit the YouTube channel at http://www.youtube.com/user/ricsil2037. This video will show you how you can get a free Virtual Phone Number (VOIP). A voip number is a phone number that uses the internet to place and receive calls.", "raw_output": "To get a free VoIP service and phone number, you can visit the YouTube channel at http://www.youtube.com/user/ricsil2037. This video will show you how you can get a free Virtual Phone Number (VOIP). A voip number is a phone number that uses the internet to place and receive calls.", "gt": "To get a free VoIP service and phone number, you can visit YouTube channels which provide tutorials on how to access these services, such as the video available at http://www.youtube.com/user/ricsil2037. You could also use cloud VoIP services that require no equipment on your end. These services offer toll-free and US local numbers that can be forwarded to any US number or used with SIP devices for outgoing calls. Additionally, companies offer DID or incoming numbers from around the world either for a flat yearly rate or a monthly fee.", "question": "how to get free voip service and phone number", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 14.258, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 68, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 264, 1910, 28079, 3298, 2473, 323, 4540, 1372, 11, 498, 646, 3947, 279, 13370, 5496, 518, 1758, 1110, 2136, 20145, 905, 11739, 14, 6198, 321, 17, 15, 18, 22, 13, 1096, 2766, 686, 1473, 498, 1246, 498, 646, 633, 264, 1910, 20721, 14307, 5624, 320, 11169, 3298, 568, 362, 4069, 573, 1372, 374, 264, 4540, 1372, 429, 5711, 279, 7602, 311, 1992, 323, 5258, 6738, 13], "logp_list": [-0.6592, -0.0675, -0.6948, -0.0029, -0.1415, -0.003, -0.0127, -0.0078, -0.0521, -0.0002, -0.0055, -0.2741, -0.0625, -0.7728, -0.779, -0.5303, -0.003, -0.5411, -0.1442, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.4871, -0.0007, -0.5931, -0.4342, -0.0733, -0.0247, -0.0982, -0.0007, -0.0011, -0.0867, -0.0005, -0.002, -0.0017, -0.0008, -0.0034, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0221, -0.017, -0.0001, -0.1049, -0.3609, -0.0219, -0.0171, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0288], "cumulative_logprob": -7.1423, "norm_logp": -0.105, "input_len": 510, "output_tokens": 68, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "691", "pred": "No, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score.", "raw_output": "No, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not directly increase your Snapchat score. The score is primarily based on the number of snaps sent and received.", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 2.417, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 11, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2753, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 697, 5456, 13], "logp_list": [-0.2769, -1.3173, -0.1314, -0.0041, -0.0054, -0.0334, -0.0006, -0.0332, -0.7103, -0.3147, -0.0296], "cumulative_logprob": -2.8569, "norm_logp": -0.2597, "input_len": 416, "output_tokens": 11, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "696", "pred": "Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen,", "raw_output": "Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen,", "gt": "To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for about 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours to ripen.", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.786, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 63, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [42178, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 11, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 11, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 13963, 594, 17961, 11, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 3197, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 304, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 11, 220], "logp_list": [-1.0913, -0.1665, -0.0016, -0.0013, -0.0018, -0.002, -0.0066, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0023, -0