{"id": "38", "pred": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees f (175 degrees c). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off", "raw_output": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees f (175 degrees c). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.517, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 53, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 282, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 272, 568, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 13, 52074, 304, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 11999, 23387, 1007], "logp_list": [-0.9853, -0.0022, -0.3049, -0.0235, -0.0138, -0.2225, -0.0016, -0.0008, -0.0087, -0.1057, -0.0619, -0.002, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0089, -0.1674, -0.2041, -0.0547, -0.0035, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0006, -0.0157, -0.0284, -0.0067, -0.0075, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0114, -0.0053, -0.169, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0044, -0.0016, -0.0011, -0.0027, -0.0003, -0.0047, -0.0047, -0.1504, -0.0283, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -2.6237, "norm_logp": -0.0495, "input_len": 267, "output_tokens": 53, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "43", "pred": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "raw_output": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic is still difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun before attempting to scrape it off. However, if the plastic cannot be removed completely, it may be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 24.054, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 120, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [6727, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 304, 6291, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 13], "logp_list": [-1.648, -0.004, -0.0002, -0.0025, -0.0014, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0015, -0.0016, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0417, -0.0007, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.1027, -0.1711, -0.0, -0.006, -0.0003, -0.0033, -0.0048, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.008, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0353, -0.4267, -0.0497, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0155, -0.0001, -0.0045, -0.094, -0.0112, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0017, -0.0144, -0.0056, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.1069, -0.1356, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0519, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0038, -0.0026, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1849, -0.0032, -0.004, -0.0104, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7647, -0.0768, -0.0028, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0038, -0.0281, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.003, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0016, -0.0007, -0.0424], "cumulative_logprob": -4.1081, "norm_logp": -0.0342, "input_len":