{"id": "62", "pred": "To set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right hand corner of the browser window.\n3", "raw_output": "To set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right hand corner of the browser window.\n3", "gt": "Method 1 of 2 in passage 2 provides the steps to set the default web browser in Windows 7.", "question": "set default browser to windows", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 9.899, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 50, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 738, 34733, 25929, 438, 697, 1638, 5515, 6929, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 697, 25929, 6929, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 25929, 5022, 3137, 11, 15251, 553, 2326, 16202, 5128, 323, 7407, 304, 279, 8416, 1290, 1424, 9131, 315, 279, 6929, 3241, 624, 18, 198], "logp_list": [-1.3888, -0.0048, -1.3062, -0.0021, -0.0083, -0.2153, -0.0003, -0.1215, -0.0063, -0.159, -0.6282, -0.0806, -0.0043, -0.5415, -0.0757, -0.0213, -0.045, -0.0538, -0.0135, -0.0003, -0.0878, -0.002, -0.0004, -0.0028, -0.0047, -0.0004, -0.0076, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.3508, -0.2655, -0.0009, -0.0054, -0.0052, -0.0965, -0.2418, -0.0028, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0054, -0.206, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0021, -0.0003, -0.9397, -0.0193, -0.4337], "cumulative_logprob": -7.3619, "norm_logp": -0.1472, "input_len": 383, "output_tokens": 50, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.82, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "67", "pred": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag", "raw_output": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn US flag is to either:\n\n1. Burn it in a peaceful manner, removing the blue field first and burying the ashes, or\n2. Perform a proper ceremony by folding the flag in a triangle fold before burning it.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: \"Option 1 or Option 2.\"", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 2.117, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 10, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181], "logp_list": [-0.8823, -0.0292, -0.0072, -0.0018, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.0004, -0.3738, -0.0009], "cumulative_logprob": -1.2988, "norm_logp": -0.1299, "input_len": 246, "output_tokens": 10, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.81, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "75", "pred": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. When hot, lightly oil grate. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer; add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper. Pr", "raw_output": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. When hot, lightly oil grate. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer; add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper. Pr", "gt": "Based on the passages provided, the steps to cook brats are as follows:\n\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook. \n2. Combine beer and onions in a large pot and bring it to a boil. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer, adding red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. In the meantime, preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate.\n5. After simmering, remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and reduce the heat to low, continuing to cook the onions.\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally, for about 10 to 14 minutes until they are browned evenly.\n7. Serve the bratwurst with the beer and onion mixture as a topping or side.", "question": "how to cook brats", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 11.429, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 58, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 13, 3197, 4017, 11, 33404, 5590, 85354, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 26, 912, 279, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 13, 2340], "logp_list": [-1.645, -0.0047, -0.4337, -0.003, -0.0005, -0.01, -0.002, -0.0022, -0.0004, -0.1014, -0.7771, -0.0237, -0.0026, -0.0006, -0.0008, -0.3586, -0.0145, -0.2088, -0.0037, -0.0016, -0.0036, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0029, -0.0105, -0.0029, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0024, -0.1036, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0026, -0.1035, -0.0123, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0567, -0.0017, -0.0013, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.0084, -0.3587], "cumulative_logprob": -4.276, "norm_logp": -0.0737, "input_len": 524, "output_tokens": 58, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "80", "pred": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, alternating diarrhea and constipation, belly pains or cramps, and a lot of gas or bloating. The cause of IBS is currently unknown, but it is thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract.", "raw_output": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, alternating diarrhea and constipation, belly pains or cramps, and a lot of gas or bloating. The cause of IBS is currently unknown, but it is thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract.", "gt": "The cause of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is unknown. However, it is believed to be a result of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in communication between the brain and the GI tract, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors may include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (either too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include diarrhea, constipation, or alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps that worsen after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, as well as a lot of gas or bloating.", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 17.21, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 79, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 358, 7347, 2924, 68293, 11, 733, 48586, 11, 72362, 68293, 323, 733, 48586, 11, 35417, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 323, 264, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 13, 576, 5240, 315, 358, 7347, 374, 5023, 9788, 11, 714, 432, 374, 3381, 311, 1102, 504, 264, 10601, 315, 34563, 79211, 320, 28034, 8, 41829, 19029, 11, 7172, 17526, 315, 47031, 5746, 11, 323, 264, 43119, 304, 279, 10535, 1948, 279, 8109, 323, 279, 48509, 41829, 13], "logp_list": [-0.7401, -0.0005, -0.3969, -0.6126, -0.0005, -0.5442, -0.0743, -0.2327, -0.0215, -0.0, -0.0172, -1.1032, -0.4939, -0.0146, -0.002, -0.0001, -0.0033, -0.0836, -0.1272, -0.0573, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.069, -0.6902, -0.8165, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0013, -0.0065, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0436, -0.3157, -0.4205, -0.0163, -0.0654, -0.0, -0.002, -0.5901, -0.0026, -0.2093, -0.0232, -0.0132, -0.0075, -0.2814, -0.0013, -0.2027, -0.0, -0.0522, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0326, -0.095, -0.661, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0048, -0.1444, -0.0022, -0.0015, -0.0081, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0105, -0.0826, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.0041, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0004, -0.0018, -0.0126], "cumulative_logprob": -9.4258, "norm_logp": -0.1193, "input_len": 335, "output_tokens": 79, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.2, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "86", "pred": "Place clean glass slide on a flat surface. Add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, and go at an angle of about 45 deg, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once", "raw_output": "Place clean glass slide on a flat surface. Add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, and go at an angle of about 45 deg, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 18.448, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 93, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [17371, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 11, 323, 728, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 5254, 11, 5796, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279,