{"id": "162", "pred": "Prostate-specific antigen, or PSA, is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man's blood.", "raw_output": "Prostate-specific antigen, or PSA, is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man's blood.", "gt": "PSA, or Prostate-specific antigen, is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. The level of PSA in a man's blood is measured by the PSA test, which involves sending a blood sample to a laboratory for analysis. The results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate conditions such as prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition like prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. Total PSA levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may indicate prostate cancer, benign prostate hyperplasia, or inflammation of the prostate.", "question": "what is psa levels mean", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.262, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 33, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1336, 2454, 18906, 81989, 11, 476, 69486, 11, 374, 264, 12833, 8947, 553, 7761, 315, 279, 46347, 66069, 13, 576, 69486, 1273, 10953, 279, 2188, 315, 69486, 304, 264, 883, 594, 6543, 13], "logp_list": [-2.3616, -0.003, -0.0194, -0.0011, -0.6731, -0.0066, -0.0006, -0.0038, -0.0281, -0.0113, -0.0386, -0.0089, -0.0004, -0.0184, -0.0029, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0285, -0.3221, -0.0182, -0.0069, -0.0061, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.0011, -0.007, -0.0008, -0.0656, -0.0003, -0.0561], "cumulative_logprob": -3.6941, "norm_logp": -0.1119, "input_len": 459, "output_tokens": 33, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "170", "pred": "Preheat oven to lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn oven off and leave sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always", "raw_output": "Preheat oven to lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn oven off and leave sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always", "gt": "To soften brown sugar, you can place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Then put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. To make hardened granulated sugar soft again, preheat an oven to its lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from its package and put it in an ovenproof container. Place it in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "question": "how to soften sugar", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 16.143, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 80, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 23387, 311, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 13, 10783, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10771, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 23387, 1007, 323, 5274, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240], "logp_list": [-0.6305, -0.0004, -0.1443, -0.0012, -0.0296, -0.0063, -0.0224, -0.0094, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0076, -0.0048, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0153, -0.015, -0.0046, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0002, -0.0012, -0.0003, -0.0049, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.0099, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0016, -0.0018, -0.0015, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0011, -0.0009, -0.0034, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.013, -0.0021, -0.0073, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.007, -0.0191, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0003, -0.0105, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0556, -0.0013, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0003, -0.0017, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0005, -0.001, -0.0087, -0.5783], "cumulative_logprob": -1.6414, "norm_logp": -0.0205, "input_len": 340, "output_tokens": 80, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "179", "pred": "To change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click Start Menu to load the Help Center.\n2. Enter Power Management Settings in the search field\n3", "raw_output": "To change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click Start Menu to load the Help Center.\n2. Enter Power Management Settings in the search field\n3", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to change the sleep time on my computer\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click the Start menu and select Control Panel.\n2. In the Control Panel, click on Power Options.\n3. In the Power Options window, click on \"Change when the computer sleeps\" on the left side of the window.\n4. In the \"Put the computer to sleep\" section, change the duration of time to the desired amount of time you want the computer to sit idle before it goes to sleep.\n5. Alternatively, you can also toggle off the option to enter Sleep mode automatically.\n\nIf you are using Windows 10, you can also search for \"Power Options\" in the taskbar search box and select it to open the Power Options window.\n\nIf you are using Windows 8.1 / Windows RT 8.1, you can move your mouse to the lower left-hand corner of the screen, right-click the Start button, and select Shut down or sign out, and then select Shut down.", "question": "how to change the sleep time on my computer", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 11.643, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 36, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 2297, 279, 6084, 882, 389, 697, 6366, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 5145, 9738, 311, 2795, 279, 11479, 5832, 624, 17, 13, 11252, 7420, 9551, 11296, 304, 279, 2711, 2070, 198, 18], "logp_list": [-0.6191, -0.0098, -0.0063, -0.0008, -0.0018, -0.0026, -0.0184, -0.0115, -0.0874, -0.5279, -0.0279, -0.0038, -0.2369, -0.1229, -0.0007, -0.6075, -0.7951, -0.0086, -0.2289, -0.0487, -0.0043, -0.0713, -0.0002, -0.083, -0.0028, -0.0001, -0.0598, -0.2397, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0022, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0004, -1.1008, -0.0018], "cumulative_logprob": -4.9351, "norm_logp": -0.1371, "input_len": 333, "output_tokens": 36, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "183", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 450°F and allow the oven to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes. Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper. Set oven to 450°F and allow the oven to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes. Season the roast with only", "raw_output": "Preheat the oven to 450°F and allow the oven to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes. Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper. Set oven to 450°F and allow the oven to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes. Season the roast with only", "gt": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 14.542, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 73, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 323, 2138, 279, 23387, 311, 855, 19963, 369, 264, 8028, 315, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 14263, 279, 57685, 448, 1172, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 12021, 714, 10077, 315, 7722, 4910, 3691, 24353, 13, 2573, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 323, 2138, 279, 23387, 311, 855, 19963, 369, 264, 8028, 315, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 14263, 279, 57685, 448, 1172], "logp_list": [-0.9827, -0.0021, -0.1565, -0.0002, -0.0083, -0.0072, -0.1403, -0.0165, -0.0003, -0.3424, -0.753, -0.1424, -0.1252, -0.0006, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0138, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0002, -0.0012, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0161, -0.1144, -0.0012, -0.0122, -0.0008, -0.0539, -0.0003, -0.002, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0224, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.7357, -0.9632, -0.1133, -0.0028, -0.001, -0.0008, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0015, -0.0249, -0.0053, -0.0076, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0112, -0.0026, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0021, -0.0763, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0006, -0.0016], "cumulative_logprob": -4.8796, "norm_logp": -0.0668, "input_len": 516, "output_tokens": 73, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "193", "pred": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "raw_output": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some steps for attaching multiple picture frames together:\n\nPassage 1: Table-Stand Grouping\nTo join two or three frames together, you can use identical frames or one larger frame as the middle piece. Place the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect, and then mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nPassage 2: Hanging Multiple Pictures Together\nBefore attaching the frames together, test different arrangements of the group of multiple pictures on the floor. Once you have decided on the layout, screw the frames to the backer board, repeating the process for each frame. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the frames and hang them on the wall to enjoy the finished result.\n\nPassage 3: Attaching Frames Together\nTo attach two frames together, place them back to back and mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. The placement should be the same distance from the bottom edge of each frame to ensure stability when the grouped pictures are placed on a table. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nIn conclusion, the recommended method for attaching multiple picture frames together involves using identical or matching frames, marking the hinge placement on the connecting sides, and attaching small hinges to join the frames together. It's also important to test different arrangements of the group of pictures on the floor before attaching the frames together, and to ensure that the frames are securely attached to the backer board before hanging them on the wall.", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 5.814, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 12, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [30485, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13], "logp_list": [-0.9318, -0.23, -0.0381, -0.0002, -0.0078, -0.0023, -0.3973, -0.0006, -0.0013, -0.0068, -0.0096, -0.1204], "cumulative_logprob": -1.7462, "norm_logp": -0.1455, "input_len": 471, "output_tokens": 12, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "199", "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria. Some of these bacteria also cause infections such as strep throat and impetigo. Usually", "raw_output": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria. Some of these bacteria also cause infections such as strep throat and impetigo. Usually", "gt": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused primarily by bacteria, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci, also known as Streptococcus pyogenes. This is the same bacteria that causes strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria types, such as staphylococcus, are also associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. Prior trauma, such as a cut or scrape, insect bite, burn, or needle puncture wound can serve as a source of infection as well as surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures. In rare cases, fungi can lead to this condition.", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 6.755, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 33, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [45, 757, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 13, 4329, 315, 1493, 23157, 1083, 5240, 28920, 1741, 438, 5412, 79, 27591, 323, 3163, 295, 7836, 13, 32967], "logp_list": [-0.8143, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.1617, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1133, -0.2699, -0.0109, -0.6044, -0.0433, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7984, -0.4523, -0.0022, -0.0053, -0.0015, -0.0147, -0.0001, -0.0293, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.019, -0.4492], "cumulative_logprob": -3.7958, "norm_logp": -0.115, "input_len": 520, "output_tokens": 33, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "206", "pred": "chard is a beet that", "raw_output": "chard is a beet that", "gt": "Based on the given passages, Swiss chard (also known as just plain chard) is a type of beet plant that has been selected for its leaf production rather than storage root formation. It produces large, tender deep green leaves with thick, crisp stalks. The leaves have a more assertive and sometimes bitter taste compared to spinach. Swiss chard is a perishable vegetable and should be stored in the refrigerator. It can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri.", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 1.477, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 6, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [331, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429], "logp_list": [-0.8295, -0.0001, -0.7496, -0.1023, -0.498, -0.5266], "cumulative_logprob": -2.7061, "norm_logp": -0.451, "input_len": 423, "output_tokens": 6, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "211", "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words", "raw_output": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, with all atoms having the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded, allowing for easy separation of the components using physical methods.", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 4.689, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 23, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 758, 1008, 4244], "logp_list": [-1.1642, -0.6867, -0.3932, -0.012, -0.0009, -0.0032, -0.0021, -0.0132, -0.0009, -0.0024, -0.0945, -0.0527, -0.0017, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0205, -0.3906, -0.1473, -0.1635], "cumulative_logprob": -3.1521, "norm_logp": -0.137, "input_len": 415, "output_tokens": 23, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "215", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adher", "raw_output": "To wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adher", "gt": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.899, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 65, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 646, 944, 633, 697, 28147, 4240, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 311, 4057, 894, 51396, 13078, 48132, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951], "logp_list": [-0.9255, -0.5418, -0.0245, -0.0002, -0.0083, -0.0197, -1.0623, -0.0433, -0.0405, -0.5628, -0.0505, -0.0032, -1.1422, -0.0689, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0028, -0.0001, -0.1504, -0.0165, -0.1155, -0.0662, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0242, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0118, -0.0002, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.3788, -0.0237, -0.0001, -0.0029, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0044, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0123, -0.0004, -0.0018, -0.0031, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.055, -0.0333, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0004, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0239], "cumulative_logprob": -5.4348, "norm_logp": -0.0836, "input_len": 328, "output_tokens": 65, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.86, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "224", "pred": "Step 1: Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet. Step 2: Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arm. Remove what's left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Step 4: Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The then end will hang freely in the air. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If", "raw_output": "Step 1: Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet. Step 2: Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arm. Remove what's left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Step 4: Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The then end will hang freely in the air. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If", "gt": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Fill the tank by turning on the water valve and then flushing the toilet. Adjust the lift chain as needed by moving the metal clip up or down a few links. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. Make sure it is securely fastened.\n6. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 42.981, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 212, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 13, 14822, 220, 17, 25, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 6773, 13, 10783, 1128, 594, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 14822, 220, 19, 25, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 13, 576, 1221, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 270