{"id": "294", "pred": "The proper way to fertilize your grass involves fertilizing at the right time of year, knowing your fertilizer to work best, you'll need to time it so that you fertilize at the beginning of the growing season. This is different for different types of grasses. F", "raw_output": "The proper way to fertilize your grass involves fertilizing at the right time of year, knowing your fertilizer to work best, you'll need to time it so that you fertilize at the beginning of the growing season. This is different for different types of grasses. F", "gt": "To properly fertilize your grass, you should fertilize at the beginning of the growing season for your specific grass type. For warm season grasses, this would be when the grass turns green in the early spring. You should also know the type of fertilizer to use based on the type of grass you have and do a pH soil test to ensure the fertilizer has the appropriate pH for your soil. Once you've determined the correct fertilizer and timing, apply it in a perpendicular pattern and check the lawn after application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, the lawn is in good shape, but if it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.69, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 55, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 35114, 4849, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 11, 14063, 697, 64291, 311, 975, 1850, 11, 498, 3278, 1184, 311, 882, 432, 773, 429, 498, 35114, 551, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 13, 1096, 374, 2155, 369, 2155, 4494, 315, 16359, 288, 13, 434], "logp_list": [-0.8373, -0.0839, -0.0024, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0564, -0.0022, -0.4877, -1.7869, -0.0014, -0.0412, -0.0002, -0.083, -0.0004, -0.0186, -0.0436, 