{"id": "298", "pred": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "raw_output": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is needed. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring hot water is always available. Alternatively, recirculating pumps can be used to rapidly pull hot water from a water heater, while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor. However, it should be noted that heat loss from the pipes can occur, requiring the water heater to use more fuel.", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.714, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 38, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 362, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3636, -0.1354, -0.0013, -0.1394, -0.0008, -0.0307, -0.0047, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0246, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.1224, -0.5183, -0.0003, -0.005, -0.0001, -0.1771, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0204], "cumulative_logprob": -2.5766, "norm_logp": -0.0678, "input_len": 298, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "302", "pred": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "raw_output": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to make a hot water heater circulate:\n\nOption 1: Install a recirculating pump. Passage 3 explains that recirculating pumps can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These pumps can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\n\nOption 2: Use a hot water circulation pump. Passage 2 describes how a hot water circulation pump can send cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, ensuring that hot water is always available when needed.\n\nIt is important to note that running a hot water circulation pump continuously can consume a significant amount of energy, as mentioned in passage 1. Therefore, it may be more cost-effective to only run the pump when needed, such as when you turn on the faucet.", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.714, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 38, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 362, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3636, -0.1354, -0.0013, -0.1394, -0.0008, -0.0307, -0.0047, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0246, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.1224, -0.5183, -0.0003, -0.005, -0.0001, -0.1771, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0204], "cumulative_logprob": -2.5766, "norm_logp": -0.0678, "input_len": 298, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.27, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
