{"id": "462", "pred": "The benefits of cupping massage include:\n\n1. Eliminates toxins: A cupping massage is an effective way", "raw_output": "The benefits of cupping massage include:\n\n1. Eliminates toxins: A cupping massage is an effective way", "gt": "Cupping massage has several benefits including eliminating toxins from the body, improved circulation, pain relief, and mental benefits such as reducing anxiety and depression.", "question": "benefits of cupping massage", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 4.498, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 23, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 7567, 315, 10525, 9989, 6245, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 42320, 258, 973, 61086, 25, 362, 10525, 9989, 6245, 374, 458, 7373, 1616], "logp_list": [-1.3198, -0.166, -0.0084, -0.06, -0.0109, -0.0454, -0.1644, -1.5595, -0.2271, -0.0491, -0.0683, -0.6891, -0.0001, -0.0026, -0.1053, -0.0573, -0.0411, -0.0014, -0.0031, -0.1221, -0.0385, -0.0003, -0.0029], "cumulative_logprob": -4.7427, "norm_logp": -0.2062, "input_len": 256, "output_tokens": 23, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "469", "pred": "Outdoor hiking has a myriad of benefits for both the body and the mind. Hiking is inexpensive and easy to start, so you can participate no matter how fit you currently are", "raw_output": "Answer: Outdoor hiking has a myriad of benefits for both the body and the mind. Hiking is inexpensive and easy to start, so you can participate no matter how fit you currently are", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here are the benefits of hiking as a hobby:\n\n1. Outdoor hiking promotes mental health (Passage 1).\n2. Hiking can help increase your levels of vitamin D through exposure to sunshine (Passage 2).\n3. Hiking has a positive impact on combating symptoms of stress and anxiety (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, the main benefits of hiking as a hobby are its positive effects on mental health, physical health, and stress reduction.", "question": "benefits of hiking as a hobby facts", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.272, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 37, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 32682, 37364, 702, 264, 51809, 315, 7567, 369, 2176, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 3971, 13, 472, 19233, 374, 43152, 323, 4135, 311, 1191, 11, 773, 498, 646, 15759, 902, 4925, 1246, 4946, 498, 5023, 525], "logp_list": [-0.9131, -0.1201, -0.913, -0.0112, -1.1703, -0.0765, -0.0077, -0.0018, -0.0002, -0.0076, -0.0009, -0.0012, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.1642, -0.8946, -0.0001, -0.0943, -0.036, -0.0037, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0348, -0.0168, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0042, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0025, -0.0026, -0.0445], "cumulative_logprob": -4.5268, "norm_logp": -0.1223, "input_len": 286, "output_tokens": 37, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.3, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "474", "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is that refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also called pure or virgin coconut oil is made from the flesh of the fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining.", "raw_output": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is that refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also called pure or virgin coconut oil is made from the flesh of the fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, while refined coconut oil loses these qualities during the refining process.\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) than unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\nTherefore, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their source, aroma, flavor, and smoking point.", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 13.104, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 66, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 374, 429, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 2598, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 279, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 429, 374, 5558, 2337, 73185, 13], "logp_list": [-0.5474, -0.2768, -0.0119, -0.0023, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0025, -0.7423, -0.6914, -0.0859, -0.0142, -0.0019, -0.4488, -0.1242, -0.0156, -0.0858, -0.0028, -0.0051, -0.0061, -0.831, -0.2941, -0.0109, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0013, -0.0003, -0.1435, -0.0046, -0.2396, -0.0005, -0.0018, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.4295, -0.0116, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.0051, -0.0021, -0.2882, -0.0199, -0.6093, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.001, -0.003, -0.0414, -0.0041, -0.0066, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0618, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0574], "cumulative_logprob": -6.1456, "norm_logp": -0.0931, "input_len": 257, "output_tokens": 66, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "481", "pred": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked due to the use of third-party apps. Snapchat cannot guarantee your security", "raw_output": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked due to the use of third-party apps. Snapchat cannot guarantee your security", "gt": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked if you have used third-party apps to access Snapchat. The company does not guarantee your security when using these apps and may send you a warning message before locking your account. If you have been warned multiple times and continue using third-party apps, your account may remain locked.", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 4.488, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 21, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [7771, 55179, 2692, 1231, 387, 27092, 16061, 4152, 311, 279, 990, 315, 4843, 24031, 10500, 13, 55179, 4157, 15440, 697, 4763], "logp_list": [-1.6514, -0.0214, -0.1446, -0.8242, -0.3304, -0.115, -0.0013, -0.6971, -0.0001, -0.2309, -0.0516, -0.0079, -0.1387, -0.0165, -0.128, -0.4931, -0.6848, -0.4079, -0.005, -0.584, -0.0593], "cumulative_logprob": -6.5932, "norm_logp": -0.314, "input_len": 496, "output_tokens": 21, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.27, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "485", "pred": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked due to the use of third-party apps. Snapchat cannot guarantee your security", "raw_output": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked due to the use of third-party apps. Snapchat cannot guarantee your security", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, it appears that your Snapchat account has been temporarily locked due to using third-party apps. According to passage 2, Snapchat does not guarantee security when using third-party apps, and they may lock your account if they detect such usage. Passage 3 also mentions that Snapchat has taken steps to punish individuals who use third-party apps, which could result in account lockout.\n\nIt's possible that you have been warned multiple times by Snapchat about using third-party apps, as mentioned in passage 1, and your account has been locked as a result. To regain access to your account, you may need to stop using third-party apps and wait for an official Snapchat app to become available for your device, as suggested in passage 2.", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 4.481, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 21, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [7771, 55179, 2692, 1231, 387, 27092, 16061, 4152, 311, 279, 990, 315, 4843, 24031, 10500, 13, 55179, 4157, 15440, 697, 4763], "logp_list": [-1.6514, -0.0214, -0.1446, -0.8242, -0.3304, -0.115, -0.0013, -0.6971, -0.0001, -0.2309, -0.0516, -0.0079, -0.1387, -0.0165, -0.128, -0.4931, -0.6848, -0.4079, -0.005, -0.584, -0.0593], "cumulative_logprob": -6.5932, "norm_logp": -0.314, "input_len": 496, "output_tokens": 21, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "491", "pred": "By using a website which is able to check the popular tweets which favorite as well as people who favorite your tweets.", "raw_output": "By using a website which is able to check the popular tweets which favorite as well as people who favorite your tweets.", "gt": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by going to Twitter.com and logging in with your Twitter username and password. Once logged in, click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, then click on Settings and finally Blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. By setting this feature, you will receive an email notification whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 4.886, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 23, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1359, 1667, 264, 3910, 892, 374, 2952, 311, 1779, 279, 5411, 23150, 892, 6930, 438, 1632, 438, 1251, 879, 6930, 697, 23150, 13], "logp_list": [-1.7138, -0.5236, -0.3438, -0.1204, -0.8167, -0.5125, -0.0077, -0.0024, -0.0257, -0.5032, -0.076, -0.0088, -0.1277, -0.5861, -0.027, -0.0022, -0.0154, -0.0229, -0.1681, -0.0569, -0.1124, -0.0073, -0.1039], "cumulative_logprob": -5.8845, "norm_logp": -0.2558, "input_len": 429, "output_tokens": 23, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "496", "pred": "Salary exchange is a way of making pension contributions that could allow both employers and employees to save money. An employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in", "raw_output": "Answer: Salary exchange is a way of making pension contributions that could allow both employers and employees to save money. An employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in", "gt": "Salary exchange pension contributions allow employees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer. This arrangement benefits both employers and employees as employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to the reduced salary, and employees can save money by making pension contributions through this method. The amount of salary waived under the salary exchange is equivalent to the regular pension contribution, and the employer pays a corresponding amount into the pension scheme. The specific details of the contributions may vary depending on the pension scheme being used.", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 6.961, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 35, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 41758, 9289, 374, 264, 1616, 315, 3259, 27681, 19026, 429, 1410, 2138, 2176, 22426, 323, 8256, 311, 3581, 3220, 13, 1527, 9364, 32908, 311, 2968, 705, 949, 315, 862, 16107, 476, 12037, 304], "logp_list": [-0.8257, -0.1094, -0.2095, -0.1931, -0.5099, -0.0105, -0.1741, -0.1425, -0.0069, -0.0014, -0.0012, -0.4035, -0.0821, -0.0031, -0.0006, -0.0036, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0003, -0.0069, -0.0018, -0.0506, -1.6597, -0.0018, -0.0361, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0846, -0.029, -0.0005, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.007, -0.0008, -0.0098], "cumulative_logprob": -4.5692, "norm_logp": -0.1305, "input_len": 467, "output_tokens": 35, "eval_