{"id": "504", "pred": "The characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of herbs and mushrooms that grow on the floor, as well as various types of", "raw_output": "The characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of herbs and mushrooms that grow on the floor, as well as various types of", "gt": "The floor of a tropical rainforest biome is characterized by a fast rate of decay due to the heat and moisture. This decay provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow. Various types of fruits, nuts, herbs, and mushrooms grow on the rainforest floor. Additionally, vines and ferns grow all over the rainforest, including the floor, helping to connect the various layers of the biome.", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.909, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 1, "n_tokens": 27, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 279, 9362, 315, 41293, 323, 47151, 429, 3063, 389, 279, 6422, 11, 438, 1632, 438, 5257, 4494, 315], "logp_list": [-0.4493, -0.4266, -0.0014, -0.2281, -0.011, -0.0005, -0.0099, -0.0092, -0.1119, -0.8695, -0.3031, -0.0005, -1.2698, -0.0016, -0.0034, -1.1532, -0.0043, -0.0887, -0.074, -0.0907, -0.3425, -0.7396, -0.0031, -0.0018, -0.0999, -0.0192, -0.0], "cumulative_logprob": -6.3128, "norm_logp": -0.2338, "input_len": 424, "output_tokens": 27, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "510", "pred": "The difference between the two is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks and", "raw_output": "The difference between the two is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks and", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that the main difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is their location within the sirloin muscle. Sirloin steaks are cut from the back of the animal and continue off the short loin from which other cuts such as T-bone and porterhouse steaks are made. On the other hand, porterhouse steaks are specifically carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin and therefore have more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to T-bone steaks. However, the passages suggest that both sirloin and porterhouse steaks may be referred to as the same thing or as a large version of the T-bone due to their similarity in appearance and taste.", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.355, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 42, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1378, 374, 429, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 5610, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 1091, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 323], "logp_list": [-0.6034, -0.1012, -0.0196, -1.0703, -0.1475, -0.0484, -0.0022, -0.0673, -0.0008, -0.0038, -0.0009, -0.0067, -0.0004, -0.0026, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0022, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0009, -0.1275, -0.0041, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0048, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0106, -0.0068, -0.0001, -0.0115, -0.0012, -0.0099, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.1018], "cumulative_logprob": -2.3663, "norm_logp": -0.0563, "input_len": 442, "output_tokens": 42, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.82, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "520", "pred": "The reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards. Your entry ticket has a number on it from 1 to approximately 55. Tickets are $50 each and a table consists of 20 individuals, which constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. and two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pull. individuals totaling twenty.", "raw_output": "The reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards. Your entry ticket has a number on it from 1 to approximately 55. Tickets are $50 each and a table consists of 20 individuals, which constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. and two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pull. individuals totaling twenty.", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's how raffles work:\n\nA reverse raffle works by having participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, usually between 1 and 55. Each ticket costs $50, and a table consists of 20 individuals who pool their money together to form a complete ticket worth $1000. There are also two $500 prizes, one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled.\n\nThe 50-50 draw is a raffle that takes place during a single event, where tickets are sold to patrons throughout the event by roaming staff. 50% of the gross proceeds go into a prize pool, and the winner of the random draw at the end of the event receives 50% of the prize pool. The remaining 50% goes to a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n\nFinally, some events may include cash tip board raffles, where participants can pay to play and have the chance to win $10,000. These raffles are not included in the ticket price.", "question": "how do raffles work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 16.183, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 82, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 9931, 435, 44090, 374, 264, 435, 44090, 714