{"id": "628", "pred": "Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities", "raw_output": "Answer: Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities", "gt": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you can stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, you can keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player and defend against them with tips from an experienced basketball player.", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.908, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 41, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 28737, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 264, 16217, 11, 25530, 31571, 979, 498, 7616, 1435, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 13, 3218, 3132, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488], "logp_list": [-0.8378, -0.0086, -0.3835, -0.1138, -0.0004, -0.0024, -0.0002, -0.0041, -0.0157, -0.001, -0.0196, -0.0001, -0.0012, -0.2426, -0.0033, -0.0024, -0.0052, -0.0015, -0.0004, -0.0015, -0.0043, -0.0001, -0.0369, -0.0162, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0058, -0.0036, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0051, -0.0004, -0.001, -0.0005], "cumulative_logprob": -1.7232, "norm_logp": -0.042, "input_len": 247, "output_tokens": 41, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.79, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "632", "pred": "Both the nervous system and endocrine system are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of of cells, tissues, organs, and systems. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs in the two systems.", "raw_output": "Both the nervous system and endocrine system are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of of cells, tissues, organs, and systems. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs in the two systems.", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system are both critical to maintaining homeostasis in the body by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. They both use chemical messengers, although their method of transmission and release differs. The nervous system is made of interconnected neuron cells and uses electrochemical pulses for signal transmission. In contrast, the endocrine system is made of discrete glands that use hormones for signal transmission and utilizes the circulatory system to carry these signals.", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.205, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 63, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [20629, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 315, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 11, 7892, 862, 1714, 315, 18368, 323, 4879, 43