{"id": "724", "pred": "The Wellesley forecast for August 22 is 82 degrees and Sunny with a 39 percentage chance of rain and 10 mph winds from the North-Northwest.", "raw_output": "Answer: The Wellesley forecast for August 22 is 82 degrees and Sunny with a 39 percentage chance of rain and 10 mph winds from the North-Northwest.", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "question": "weather in wellesley", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.928, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 41, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 576, 25006, 642, 3179, 17595, 369, 6156, 220, 17, 17, 374, 220, 23, 17, 12348, 323, 55038, 448, 264, 220, 18, 24, 11414, 6012, 315, 11174, 323, 220, 16, 15, 33961, 28492, 504, 279, 4787, 11250, 2364, 11039, 13], "logp_list": [-1.2574, -0.1471, -0.8276, -0.8774, -0.0006, -0.0012, -0.26, -0.2515, -0.2844, -0.0869, -0.1137, -0.2213, -0.371, -0.0795, -0.1435, -0.0093, -0.0005, -0.0936, -0.1279, -0.86, -0.0712, -0.0074, -0.0096, -0.0856, -0.2533, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0249, -0.0072, -0.0045, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0029, -0.0011, -0.0024, -0.0005, -0.0041, -0.0, -0.0535], "cumulative_logprob": -6.5449, "norm_logp": -0.1596, "input_len": 325, "output_tokens": 41, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "732", "pred": "The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air. This exchange happens in the lungs", "raw_output": "The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air. This exchange happens in the lungs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the process of processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs involves the following steps:\n\n1. The diaphragm muscle contracts to take air into the lungs, moving down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region. (Passage 1)\n2. The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment, occurring in the lungs. (Passage 2)\n3. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity, including the lungs, decreases the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing us to inhale. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the main steps in processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs are:\n\n1. Contraction of the diaphragm muscle to draw air into the lungs.\n2. Exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment in the lungs.\n3. Expansion of the thoracic cavity to decrease air pressure in the lungs and facilitate inhalation.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.929, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 46, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 429, 13666, 1948, 498, 11, 304, 3953, 11, 279, 7761, 315, 697, 2487, 11, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 11, 892, 374, 279, 3720, 13, 1096, 9289, 8573, 304, 279, 44174], "logp_list": [-0.2909, -0.3329, -0.1826, -0.2055, -0.0999, -0.0475, -0.0368, -0.0002, -0.0027, -0.0812, -0.08, -0.2831, -0.0153, -0.0037, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.505, -0.0069, -0.0004, -0.1588, -0.0112, -0.006, -0.0021, -0.0017, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.0038, -0.0057, -0.0011, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0013, -0.0066, -0.0076, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0061, -0.3289, -0.0006, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -2.723, "norm_logp": -0.0592, "input_len": 364, "output_tokens": 46, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "737", "pred": "SMS stands for Short Message Service and is also commonly referred to as a text message. With a SMS, you can send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will automatically be split by into several parts. Most cell phones support this type of text messaging. MMS: MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and this type of text messaging is an evolution of the SMS. With a MMS, you can send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. It is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone", "raw_output": "SMS stands for Short Message Service and is also commonly referred to as a text message. With a SMS, you can send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will automatically be split by into several parts. Most cell phones support this type of text messaging. MMS: MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and this type of text messaging is an evolution of the SMS. With a MMS, you can send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. It is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 23.53, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 121, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [65565, 13352, 369, 10698, 4856, 5362, 323, 374, 1083, 16626, 13862, 311, 438, 264, 1467, 1943, 