{"id": "20", "pred": "1. Dump a chimney of lit coals into the grill.\n2. With a grill hoe or garden hoe, spread the coals into a double layer at the far side and a single layer in the center.\n3  Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n4  Replace the grill grate.\n5  If using a gas grill, set it in for three-zone grilling.\n6  Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.", "raw_output": "1. Dump a chimney of lit coals into the grill.\n2. With a grill hoe or garden hoe, spread the coals into a double layer at the far side and a single layer in the center.\n3  Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n4  Replace the grill grate.\n5  If using a gas grill, set it in for three-zone grilling.\n6  Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not contain any information or instructions on how to grill a Porterhouse steak specifically. While they do provide general guidance on setting up a grill and preparing the grill grate, they do not offer any specific advice or steps for cooking a Porterhouse steak. Therefore, I cannot provide a response based on the given passages.", "question": "how to grill a porterhouse", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 26.282, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 126, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16, 13, 29693, 264, 89051, 315, 13020, 1062, 1127, 1119, 279, 39058, 624, 17, 13, 3085, 264, 39058, 45876, 476, 13551, 45876, 11, 8865, 279, 1062, 1127, 1119, 264, 1990, 6193, 518, 279, 3041, 3108, 323, 264, 3175, 6193, 304, 279, 4126, 624, 18, 2