{"id": "26", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. The", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. The", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not mention anything about Magellan of Virginia's status as a provider or its relationship with other providers. Passage 1 discusses Magellan's ability to offer continuing education credits, while Passage 2 explains its role as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Passage 3 mentions a weekly call for providers to ask questions and address issues, but it does not provide information about Magellan's status as a provider. Therefore, I cannot answer the question based on the given passages.", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 5.231, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 26, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 18432, 264, 17059, 1618, 1817, 6602, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 481, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 576], "logp_list": [-0.1184, -0.0005, -0.0853, -0.0002, -2.4595, -0.2441, -0.002, -0.0353, -0.0432, -0.0002, -0.0127, -0.0007, -0.0006, -0.0439, -0.0014, -0.0283, -0.1315, -0.0014, -0.0003, -0.0037, -0.1351, -0.2217, -0.0046, -0.0003, -0.0239, -0.424], "cumulative_logprob": -4.0228, "norm_logp": -0.1547, "input_len": 319, "output_tokens": 26, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "31", "pred": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry on the jamb until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from it's original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "raw_output": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry on the jamb until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from it's original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check the door stop: According to passage 2, if the door won't lock, try tapping the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Then, place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\n2. Adjust the latch hole: If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb, as suggested in passage 3. Before doing so, tighten the hinges first. Additionally, you may need to enlarge the strike plate hole and move the strike plate.\n\nIf the passages do not provide sufficient information to answer the question, the response would be: \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 45.464, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 2, "n_tokens": 139, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 432, 594, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13], "logp_list": [-2.1908, -0.0041, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.0078, -0.0058, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0216, -0.0461, -0.0049, -0.0107, -0.0706, -0.0023, -0.2896, -0.03, -0.0062, -0.0001, -0.4524, -0.0453, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0064, -0.0441, -0.0152, -0.0043, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0033, -0.0016, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0416, -0.0055, -0.7497, -0.1196, -1.1651, -0.0003, -0.2099, -0.1528, -0.0153, -0.0024, -0.1529, -0.0148, -0.0908, -0.0162, -0.01, -0.0271, -0.033, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0022, -0.0006, -0.0073, -0.0026, -0.0104, -0.0792, -0.0519, -0.0003, -0.6003, -0.2231, -0.0114, -0.0039, -0.0234, -0.0044, -0.0074, -0.0339, -0.0019, -0.0008, -0.0233, -0.009, -0.0085, -0.0019, -0.0277, -0.0029, -0.0022, -0.0023, -0.0045, -0.0016, -0.7059, -0.0107, -0.0018, -0.0048, -0.0049, -0.2475, -0.0085, -0.0022, -0.0004, -0.022