{"id": "39", "pred": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "raw_output": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "gt": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior. You can then apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Afterward, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. You can mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. Some plastic may be extremely difficult to remove, in which case you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun and then peel it off. If not all plastic comes off, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 24.158, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 120, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [6727, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 304, 6291, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 13], "logp_list": [-1.648, -0.004, -0.0002, -0.0025, -0.0014, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0015, -0.0016, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0417, -0.0007, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.1027, -0.1711, -0.0, -0.006, -0.0003, -0.0033, -0.0048, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.008, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0353, -0.4267, -0.0497, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0155, -0.0001, -0.0045, -0.094, -0.0112, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0017, -0.0144, -0.0056, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.1069, -0.1356, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0519, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0038, -0.0026, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1849, -0.0032, -0.004, -0.0104, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7647, -0.0768, -0.0028, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0038, -0.0281, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.003, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0016, -0.0007, -0.0424], "cumulative_logprob": -4.1081, "norm_logp": -0.0342, "input_len": 584, "output_tokens": 120, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 72.94, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "44", "pred": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "raw_output": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic does not come off with this method, another option is to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic until it becomes soft and pliable. Then, attempt to peel it off carefully. However, be aware that this method may not work, and in that case, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. It is recommended to call a service technician for this type of repair.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to get plastic out of clothes dryer is:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper.\n3. Apply nail polish remover to dissolve the plastic.\n4. Rinse with a damp cloth and soap solution.\n5. Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic if necessary.\n\nIf the plastic still does not come off, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer.", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 24.274, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 120, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [6727, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 304, 6291, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 13], "logp_list": [-1.648, -0.004, -0.0002, -0.0025, -0.0014, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0015, -0.0016, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0417, -0.0007, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.1027, -0.1711, -0.0, -0.006, -0.0003, -0.0033, -0.0048, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.008, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0353, -0.4267, -0.0497, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0155, -0.0001, -0.0045, -0.094, -0.0112, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0017, -0.0144, -0.0056, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.1069, -0.1356, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0519, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0038, -0.0026, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1849, -0.0032, -0.004, -0.0104, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7647, -0.0768, -0.0028, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0038, -0.0281, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.003, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0016, -0.0007, -0.0424], "cumulative_logprob": -4.1081, "norm_logp": -0.0342, "input_len": 584, "output_tokens": 120, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.2, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "49", "pred": "Step 1: Lay your quilt on a bed, table or or flat surface. Step 2: Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 3: Fold the lower left corner on toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 4: Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 5: Making sure the fold is on the bias, fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt.", "raw_output": "Step 1: Lay your quilt on a bed, table or or flat surface. Step 2: Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 3: Fold the lower left corner on toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 4: Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt making sure the fold is on the bias. Step 5: Making sure the fold is on the bias, fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fold a quilt:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n5. Fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How to fold a quilt\" can be summarized in five steps:\n\n1. Lay the quilt flat.\n2. Fold lower right corner up.\n3. Fold lower left corner up.\n4. Fold top left corner down.\n5. Fold top right corner down.", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 25.284, "status": "suc