: "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "53", "pred": "Benefits of a Water Pik include helping to maintain good oral health by massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and cleaning better around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas area that brushing can not access.", "raw_output": "Benefits of a Water Pik include helping to maintain good oral health by massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and cleaning better around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas area that brushing can not access.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the benefits of using a water pick (also known as a Waterpik) include:\n\n1. Helping to keep teeth, gums, mouth, and overall body healthier by eliminating germs and plaque.\n2. Being a great oral care tool for removing food from areas that brushing cannot access.\n3. Massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth to reduce the risk of gingivitis.\n4. Being an alternative to flossing and potentially offering similar benefits.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on other potential benefits of using a water pick, such as its ability to reach areas between teeth or its effectiveness in reducing plaque buildup.", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.251, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 51, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [84323, 315, 264, 9959, 61162, 2924, 10476, 311, 10306, 1661, 20655, 2820, 553, 3072, 4118, 323, 64692, 8413, 19847, 304, 279, 10780, 11, 17719, 279, 5214, 315, 66093, 344, 19435, 11, 323, 15826, 2664, 2163, 279, 17832, 323, 97654, 11, 17592, 3607, 504, 5671, 3082, 429, 76726, 646, 537, 2615, 13], "logp_list": [-0.957, -0.0222, -0.0504, -0.6937, -0.0923, -0.1737, -1.2009, -0.0543, -0.1234, -0.0105, -0.0006, -0.0071, -0.9985, -0.0459, -0.0001, -0.0013, -0.0021, -0.0145, -0.0077, -0.0879, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.1508, -0.3905, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0561, -0.0151, -0.0016, -0.0102, -0.0629, -0.0546, -0.5864, -0.0069, -0.0183, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.3838, -0.0056, -0.7797, -0.0236, -0.4799, -0.3745, -0.0033, -0.0545, -0.1567, -0.0039, -0.0033, -0.018], "cumulative_logprob": -8.1859, "norm_logp": -0.1605, "input_len": 317, "output_tokens": 51, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "58", "pred": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. The netting keep the birds from reaching those spaces they often", "raw_output": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. The netting keep the birds from reaching those spaces they often", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. This will prevent birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests, which can block your ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease. (Passage 1:4)\n2. Install bird netting over the top of your light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is non-flammable and safe to use around light bulbs, and make sure it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. (Passage 2:1)\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds away from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch. Move the plastic hawk periodically to keep the birds from becoming accustomed to its presence. (Passage 3:1)\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, you can keep birds from building nests on your porch by using bird netting, installing bird netting over your light fixture, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 11.118, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 55, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [30485, 11958, 4179, 1280, 311, 279, 384, 2342, 2163, 279, 46342, 315, 697, 44647, 448, 264, 48956, 6038, 13, 1416, 697, 44647, 702, 1787, 52455, 388, 11, 990, 279, 48956, 6038, 311, 15498, 279, 4179, 1280, 311, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 44647, 13, 576, 4179, 1280, 2506, 279, 19654, 504, 18739, 1846, 12621, 807, 3545], "logp_list": [-0.3129, -0.29, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0616, -0.0084, -0.0129, -0.0011, -0.0539, -0.0083, -0.0041, -0.0039, -0.0122, -0.0001, -0.0939, -0.0006, -0.0012, -0.002, -0.2395, -0.8537, -0.0052, -0.0006, -0.0546, -0.0146, -0.0007, -0.0009, -0.0014, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0112, -0.3131, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.1984, -0.0015, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0008, -0.0004, -0.0011, -0.0019], "cumulative_logprob": -2.5741, "norm_logp": -0.0468, "input_len": 422, "output_tokens": 55, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "63", "pred": "To set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right hand corner of the browser window.\n3", "raw_output": "To set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right hand corner of the browser window.\n3", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser to Windows:\n\nMethod 1:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and then clicking the Settings icon, or by using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the Settings app, click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\n\nAlternatively, you can also set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser by following these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "question": "set default browser to windows", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.023, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 50, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 738, 34733, 25929, 438, 697, 1638, 5515, 6929, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 697, 25