{"id": "112", "pred": "The Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles. They’re called the Leeward Islands because they’re away from the wind (“lee”).", "raw_output": "The Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles. They’re called the Leeward Islands because they’re away from the wind (“lee”).", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between the Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands is their exposure to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and are therefore wetter and receive more rainfall, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, but still receive some rainfall. Additionally, the Windward Islands are located southeast of the Caribbean Sea, while the Leeward Islands are located northwest of the Caribbean Sea.", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.811, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 32, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 315, 279, 13907, 6755, 30255, 13, 2379, 3129, 2598, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 1576, 807, 3129, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 26087, 8501, 64212], "logp_list": [-0.1224, -1.8214, -0.0002, -0.0688, -0.2357, -0.0877, -0.1187, -0.0015, -0.0018, -0.0195, -0.0018, -0.0052, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.2047, -0.4356, -0.1248, -0.0043, -0.0016, -0.0067, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0018, -0.0008, -0.0004, -0.0037, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0066, -0.0576, -0.0066, -0.1678], "cumulative_logprob": -3.5094, "norm_logp": -0.1097, "input_len": 285, "output_tokens": 32, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "116", "pred": "A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.", "raw_output": "A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how water shares are transferred:\n\n1. Passage 1 states that a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. The passage also mentions that a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n2. Passage 2 outlines the steps required to transfer a Water Stock Certificate: (a) The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate, (b) the new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership, (c) a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and (d) a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner.\n3. Passage 3 provides general information about buying a home with water shares or rights, including the need to understand the steps involved in transferring water rights into the buyer's name. However, this passage does not provide specific instructions for transferring water shares.\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, the answer to the question is:\n\nTransferring water shares involves paying a fee of $75.00 to process the transfer, returning the Water Stock Certificate to the company, providing proof of ownership, and obtaining a new Water Stock Certificate in the new owner's name.", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.197, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 20, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32, 11060, 315, 400, 22, 20, 13, 15, 15, 1969, 387, 7171, 311, 1882, 264, 9959, 12648, 31402, 8317, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3381, -0.3324, -0.0026, -0.014, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.009, -0.0021, -0.0002, -0.0095, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0407, -0.0184, -0.0026, -0.0124, -0.0005, -0.0029, -0.0054, -0.1015], "cumulative_logprob": -1.894, "norm_logp": -0.0947, "input_len": 333, "output_tokens": 20, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.07, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "120", "pred": "The name Teresa is a Greek baby name. In Greek, the meaning of the name Teresa is: Reap; from Therasia.", "raw_output": "The name Teresa is a Greek baby name. In Greek, the meaning of the name Teresa is: Reap; from Therasia.", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek origin and means \"Reap; from Therasia\" or \"Harvester\". It is also a Spanish and Italian name and is associated with two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The name Theresa is a variation of Teresa and also means \"Reaper; from Therasia\". The etymology of the name is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek words \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "question": "teresa name meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 5.765, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 28, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 829, 63440, 374, 264, 17860, 8770, 829, 13, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 63440, 374, 25, 1032, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 13], "logp_list": [-0.7573, -0.2003, -0.0535, -1.1978, -0.2488, -0.0222, -0.1235, -0.0002, -0.8159, -0.0703, -0.0033, -0.3173, -0.1427, -0.0191, -0.006, -0.024, -0.0001, -0.0136, -0.0021, -0.6642, -0.0979, -0.0006, -0.0139, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0334], "cumulative_logprob": -4.8288, "norm_logp": -0.1725, "input_len": 504, "output_tokens": 28, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "126", "pred": "To build a lean-to shed, first prepare the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel. Cut the two 4 x 4 skids at 7/4″. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7/4″ and six joists at 44 1/4″. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean to shed plans. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "raw_output": "To build a lean-to shed, first prepare the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel. Cut the two 4 x 4 skids at 7/4″. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7/4″ and six joists at 44 1/4″. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean to shed plans. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 25.366, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 126, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1936, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 1156, 10549, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 21580, 61