{"id": "233", "pred": "The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by an annual precipitation of 34 inches, with an average of 256 sunny days per year. The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees, while the lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees. The", "raw_output": "The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by an annual precipitation of 34 inches, with an average of 256 sunny days per year. The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees, while the lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees. The", "gt": "The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and the lowest is 50 degrees in December. The city gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January. Snowfall is non-existent. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees and the January low is 43. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, however, the pollution index is 61% worse.", "question": "average weather sausalito", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 11.897, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 60, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 31871, 553, 458, 9775, 59950, 315, 220, 18, 19, 14924, 11, 448, 458, 5461, 315, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 13, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6122, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 11, 1393, 279, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6652, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 13, 576], "logp_list": [-0.8445, -0.1514, -0.3684, -0.07, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0001, -1.1775, -0.4311, -0.0145, -1.0855, -0.6424, -0.2925, -0.0137, -0.0087, -0.0206, -0.065, -0.0027, -0.0818, -0.4838, -1.3566, -0.1006, -0.6425, -0.0053, -0.3536, -0.1888, -0.0073, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0543, -0.0001, -0.1406, -0.1341, -0.7461, -0.2903, -0.0217, -0.0021, -0.7097, -0.2266, -0.0183, -0.022, -0.0059, -0.0038, -0.0003, -0.014, -0.1902, -0.0048, -0.0025, -0.1715, -0.0005, -0.0041, -0.3212, -0.0044, -0.0126, -0.0003, -0.0057, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.6645], "cumulative_logprob": -12.1849, "norm_logp": -0.2031, "input_len": 429, "output_tokens": 60, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "242", "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps or pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out.", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps or pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are made of a metal cage with a system of nets inside, which are designed to allow crabs to enter but not escape. The traps have two leads that angle into the pot from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit entrance. The crabs crawl up the leads to reach the bait inside the pot, but cannot exit through the slit. The pot is designed to keep the crabs inside until they can be retrieved by the fisherman.\n\nAdditionally, according to passage 3, crab pots can be equipped with mechanisms that disable them over time, preventing them from continuing to catch crabs after they have been abandoned or become lost. These mechanisms can include biodegradable mesh or dissolvable cords.", "question": "how do crab traps work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 9.352, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 46, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16001, 370, 44560, 975, 553, 1667, 264, 1849, 315, 52457, 4766, 264, 3460, 9317, 35360, 1865, 315, 9067, 476, 10063, 9317, 11294, 429, 374, 48580, 448, 9509, 15904, 13, 576, 44560, 476, 50031, 525, 6188, 311, 2138, 1560, 3435, 304, 714, 537, 1077, 1105, 700, 13], "logp_list": [-0.3833, -0.0005, -0.0615, -0.3189, -0.0738, -0.1634, -0.0418, -0.035, -0.0019, -0.0011, -0.01, -0.0066, -0.0069, -0.0058, -0.0003, -0.1865, -0.004, -0.0012, -0.0057, -0.0203, -0.0027, -0.0007, -0.0651, -0.0771, -0.0025, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0444, -0.2319, -0.2897, -0.5523, -0.0004, -0.0163, -0.0085, -0.0006, -0.0016, -0.0902, -0.002, -0.0025, -0.0087, -0.0016, -0.4367, -0.023, -0.0057, -0.1], "cumulative_logprob": -3.2952, "norm_logp": -0.0716, "input_len": 450, "output_tokens": 46, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "246", "pred": "The difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like", "raw_output": "The difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) are:\n\n1. Scope of application: The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\n2. Definition of disability: The FEHA requires that a disability must limit a major life activity, while the ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity.\n3. Number of employees: The ADA applies to employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA has no such requirement.\n\nTherefore, the main difference between FEHA and ADA is the scope of application and the definition of disability.", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.991, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 45, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 279, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 19853, 279, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 11, 323, 432, 3171, 1405, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 1075], "logp_list": [-1.3182, -0.8005, -0.0169, -0.4456, -0.0004, -0.1145, -0.0574, -0.1809, -0.0329, -0.7643, -0.1017, -0.0341, -0.015, -0.2216, -0.0129, -0.0103, -0.0056, -0.0012, -0.0016, -0.0424, -0.0216, -0.0026, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0011, -0.0367, -0.0292, -0.0144, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0148, -0.0015, -0.0011, -0.038, -0.0055, -0.0019, -0.0007, -0.5937, -0.0043, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0012, -0.0012, -0.0186], "cumulative_logprob": -4.9687, "norm_logp": -0.1104, "input_len": 266, "output_tokens": 45, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "251", "pred": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavor flavor until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops that indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "raw_output": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavor flavor until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops that indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to the instructions provided in Allrecipes.com, follow these steps: \n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat. \n2. Lightly oil the grate. \n3. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until well combined. \n4. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle them with the spice mixture on both sides. \n5. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. \n6. Grill the chops over indirect heat for about 12 minutes per side, or until they are no longer pink inside.", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 21.87, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 109, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 