{"id": "272", "pred": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, and cramping.", "raw_output": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, and cramping.", "gt": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, cramping, nausea, and vomiting.", "question": "earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 5.257, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 23, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 29658, 11929, 323, 13495, 315, 19636, 2924, 19671, 56790, 11, 294, 96645, 11, 14211, 1095, 11, 89219, 11, 323, 1560, 30457, 13], "logp_list": [-1.0548, -0.0545, -0.026, -0.2524, -0.0001, -0.002, -0.0005, -0.8654, -0.2322, -0.0005, -0.1702, -0.263, -0.0002, -0.013, -0.8271, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0023, -0.0039, -0.388, -0.0008, -0.0005, -0.0244], "cumulative_logprob": -4.1829, "norm_logp": -0.1819, "input_len": 259, "output_tokens": 23, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 91.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "280", "pred": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition that virtually no symptoms until severe bone damage has already occurred. Once the bones have been weakened by bone density loss, symptoms may include: 1  Back pain.2  Loss of height over time with stooped posture. 3  Fractures of the vertebrae, wrists,", "raw_output": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition that virtually no symptoms until severe bone damage has already occurred. Once the bones have been weakened by bone density loss, symptoms may include: 1  Back pain.2  Loss of height over time with stooped posture. 3  Fractures of the vertebrae, wrists,", "gt": "Based on the given passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a advanced stage of the disease where the bones have weakened significantly, leading to severe bone loss and increased risk of fractures. At this stage, symptoms such as back pain, loss of height, and fractures are more pronounced and frequent. The risk of fractures is particularly high in the spine, hips, and wrists, and can occur even without a fall or injury.\n\nIn summary, severe osteoporosis is characterized by significant bone weakening, heightened risk of fractures, and more pronounced symptoms.", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 13.824, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 67, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1514, 19289, 51268, 88666, 10704, 374, 264, 2971, 429, 21214, 902, 13495, 3080, 15386, 17240, 5557, 702, 2669, 10017, 13, 9646, 279, 24854, 614, 1012, 57664, 553, 17240, 17457, 4709, 11, 13495, 1231, 2924, 25, 220, 16, 220, 6841, 6646, 13, 17, 220, 24704, 315, 2608, 916, 882, 448, 42032, 16367, 47278, 13, 220, 18, 220, 2869, 531, 1413, 315, 279, 5198, 50213, 68, 11, 85778, 11], "logp_list": [-0.4546, -0.0003, -0.0059, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.8968, -1.1135, -0.0109, -0.8744, -0.9025, -0.1524, -0.0012, -0.0264, -0.024, -0.0027, -0.0043, -0.3608, -0.0198, -0.0009, -0.0204, -0.9922, -0.001, -0.0013, -0.0027, -0.0024, -0.0009, -0.0021, -0.0015, -0.0009, -0.0021, -0.0429, -0.0109, -0.0045, -0.0022, -0.1969, -0.2691, -0.0063, -0.6287, -0.0171, -0.0005, -0.0263, -0.1728, -0.0076, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.4116, -0.0186, -0.0009, -0.0035, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0016, -0.1337, -0.1884, -0.1076, -0.0018, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0006, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -8.1387, "norm_logp": -0.1215, "input_len": 500, "output_tokens": 67, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "289", "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.Next, cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking.When internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for  30 minutes before serving.", "raw_output": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.Next, cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking.When internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for  30 minutes before serving.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\nPassage 1 states to defrost the roast first and then place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour. After taking it out, season the roast and turn the oven temperature to 350°F. Cook for 1.5 to 3 hours, depending on the size of the roast, making sure it's cooked all the way through.\n\nPassage 2 provides specific instructions for preparing the roast before cooking. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and any desired herbs. Place the roast in a preheated oven at 325°F and determine the cooking time based on the weight of the roast.\n\nPassage 3 suggests starting by preheating the oven to 350°F and then placing the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on a roasting rack. Cook for 20-30 minutes per pound, inserting a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature once cooked. Once the temperature reaches 150°F, remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 30 minutes before slicing and serving.\n\nBased on these passages, the general steps to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven are:\n\n1. Defrost the roast if not already thawed.\n2. Season the roast with salt, pepper, and herbs.\n3. Place the roast in a preheated oven at the appropriate temperature (250°F or 325°F) for the specified time.\n4. Check the internal temperature of the roast using a meat thermometer to ensure it reaches the desired doneness.\n5. Remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 30 minutes before slicing and serving.", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 26.199, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 127, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1191, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10224, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 18501, 11, 4296, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 11, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 50761, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 374, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 11, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13], "logp_list": [-0.7936, -0.0121, -0.0025, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0119, -0.0258, -0.0031, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0656, -0.5686, -0.0014, -0.0133, -0.002, -0.0, -0.0197, -0.0001, -0.0153, -0.0045, -0.1179, -0.0241, -0.0002, -0.0037, -0.0285, -0.0136, -0.2243, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0