{"id": "299", "pred": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "raw_output": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be installed. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater to keep it hot. This continuous loop ensures that hot water is always available.", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.857, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 38, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 362, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3636, -0.1354, -0.0013, -0.1394, -0.0008, -0.0307, -0.0047, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0246, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.1224, -0.5183, -0.0003, -0.005, -0.0001, -0.1771, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0204], "cumulative_logprob": -2.5766, "norm_logp": -0.0678, "input_len": 298, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.41, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "303", "pred": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "raw_output": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"how to make hot water heater circulate\":\n\nA hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate water through the hot water heater and ensure that hot water is always available. The pump sends cooled water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line and circulates it through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to activate the pump and circulate the water.", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.785, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 38, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 362, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3636, -0.1354, -0.0013, -0.1394, -0.0008, -0.0307, -0.0047, -0.0001, -0.023, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0246, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.1224, -0.5183, -0.0003, -0.005, -0.0001, -0.1771, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0204], "cumulative_logprob": -2.5766, "norm_logp": -0.0678, "input_len": 298, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 