{"id": "334", "pred": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.", "raw_output": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 9.274, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 43, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [10253, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3101, -0.0523, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0176, -0.0068, -0.0013, -0.0053, -0.0275, -0.0101, -0.0025, -0.0302, -0.0031, -0.0102, -0.0075, -0.0046, -0.0018, -0.1352, -0.2894, -0.0031, -0.1318, -0.0044, -0.0027, -0.0025, -0.0062, -0.0068, -0.0031, -0.0013, -0.0029, -0.0029, -0.0016, -0.0566, -0.0466, -0.002, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0019, -0.0014, -0.0015, -0.0493], "cumulative_logprob": -2.2466, "norm_logp": -0.0522, "input_len": 479, "output_tokens": 43, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "339", "pred": "To make ribs, follow these steps:\n\n1.Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\n2.Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side down on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another", "raw_output": "To make ribs, follow these steps:\n\n1.Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\n2.Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side down on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Then, brush both sides of the ribs with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it sticks to the meat. Next, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and place the ribs on the grill, meaty-side up. Brush the ribs with sauce, cover the grill, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip the ribs, brush with more sauce, and cook for another 5 minutes. Repeat this process, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "question": "how to make ribs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 15.149, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 76, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 51325, 266, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 17, 13270, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 1495, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220], "logp_list": [-0.4448,