{"id": "410", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "raw_output": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Torn pieces of bread are pushed through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n3. The crumbs are spread on a baking sheet.\n4. The sheet is baked in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. The sheet is shaken twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. After baking, the crumbs are removed from the oven and allowed to cool completely.\n\nAlternatively, according to passage 2, you can also make panko crumbs by:\n\n1. Pushing chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n2. Spreading the crumbs on a baking sheet and baking at 300 degrees F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n3. Shaking the sheet twice during baking.\n4. Being careful not to let the crumbs brown.\n\nFinally, passage 3 provides a third method for making panko crumbs, which involves blending the ingredients in a blender carafe and baking them on half sheet pans until they are crisp and lightly browned.", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 22.055, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 100, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 13, 10771, 678, 315, 279, 13966, 1119, 264, 61795, 1803, 5645, 11, 3421, 323, 27235, 3080, 49247, 96577, 1352, 11, 911, 220, 17, 4420, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 220, 17, 4279, 10834, 63783, 323, 22544, 3080, 279, 96577, 1101, 3161, 311, 13876, 323, 41854, 11, 911, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 23931, 279, 96577, 389, 279, 63783, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 11, 323, 1221, 8317, 311, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 3553, 518, 3054, 9315, 369, 705, 311, 220, 17, 5555, 13], "logp_list": [-1.4774, -0.0012, -0.7185, -0.0009, -0.0165, -0.0171, -0.1491, -0.0092, -0.0007, -0.0025, -1.1114, -0.0349, -0.0389, -0.0062, -0.0131, -0.0008, -0.0023, -0.006, -0.0013, -0.0004, -0.0031, -0.0003, -0.0095, -0.0009, -0.0386, -0.001, -0.0012, -0.0018, -0.0002, -0.0015, -0.0183, -0.0017, -0.0007, -0.0023, -0.0618, -0.0049, -0.0323, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0058, -0.0009, -0.0012, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0035, -0.0006, -0.0013, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0021, -0.2343, -0.0076, -0.0012, -0.001, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.1012, -0.0741, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0008, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0013, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0097, -0.007, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0022, -0.0016, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0008, -0.0021, -0.0034, -0.0698, -0.0038, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0087], "cumulative_logprob": -4.351, "norm_logp": -0.0435, "input_len": 521, "output_tokens": 100, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "414", "pred": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Sing Sing Monsters, you need to use the Shugabush and the Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure.", "raw_output": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Sing Sing Monsters, you need to use the Shugabush and the Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure.", "gt": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you need to first obtain a Shugabush monster from the Shugabush Island. Then, hatch the eggs obtained and purchase the breeding structure. Finally, use a Shugabush and a Furcorn in the breeding structure to create a Shugabeats monster.", "question": "how do i breed a shugabeats in my singing monsters", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 13.137, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 36, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 27775, 264, 1417, 768, 8229, 1862, 304, 3017, 10833, 10833, 62708, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 990, 279, 1417, 768, 370, 1116, 323, 279, 49840, 38630, 304, 279, 1417, 768, 370, 1116, 10720, 39208, 5944, 13], "logp_list": [-0.1961, -0.0013, -0.0409, -0.0033, -0.0058, -0.0041, -0.0867, -0.1115, -0.0484, -0.0001, -0.1824, -0.0037, -0.026, -0.0994, -0.4687, -0.0204, -1.1267, -0.0188, -0.0011, -0.0065, -0.0009, -0.0044, -0.0181, -0.0118, -0.0128, -0.0015, -0.013, -0.0028, -0.006, -0.0025, -0.0011, -0.0027, -0.0036, -0.0009, -0.0015, -0.4262], "cumulative_logprob": -2.9617, "norm_logp": -0.0823, "input_len": 420, "output_tokens": 36, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.09, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "423", "pred": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other", "raw_output": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, which is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item and is mainly used for scanning items at the point of sale.", "question": "what is a upc description", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 7.235, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 36, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 25500, 5643, 6119, 320, 3124, 34, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 429, 374, 13570, 1483, 304, 279, 3639, 4180, 11, 6864, 11, 3639, 15072, 11, 8330, 11, 1532, 16911, 11, 304, 4505, 323, 1008], "logp_list": [-1.153, -0.4727, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0725, -0.002, -0.0024, -0.021, -0.0555, -0.0096, -0.0029, -0.0032, -0.0, -1.1307, -0.0105, -0.0075, -0.0003, -0.0625, -0.0587, -0.0064, -0.0008, -0.0049, -0.0005, -0.0012, -0.0097, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.001, -0.0134, -0.0003, -0.0195, -0.0898], "cumulative_logprob": -3.2154, "norm_logp": -0.0893, "input_len": 390, "output_tokens": 36, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "429", "pred": "Twins can be either monozygotic (identical), meaning that they develop from one zygote, which splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic (fraternal), meaning that they develop from two different eggs.", "raw_output": "Twins can be either monozygotic (identical), meaning that they develop from one zygote, which splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic (fraternal), meaning that they develop from two different eggs.", "gt": "Twins can happen in two ways: monozygotic (identical) twins occur when one zygote splits into two embryos, while dizygotic (fraternal) twins happen when two different eggs are fertilized by two separate sperm cells. The likelihood of dizygotic twins is influenced by factors such as West African descent, being between 30 and 40 years old, being taller and heavier than average, and having had several previous pregnancies. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the zygote happens within 8 days of fertilization and can result in complications due to shared organs.", "question": "how do twins happen", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.337, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 48, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [22816, 1330, 646, 387, 2987, 39674, 4246, 70, 14212, 320, 1713, 938, 701, 7290, 429, 807, 2225, 504, 825, 1147, 48765, 1272, 11, 892, 40467, 323, 7586, 1378, 88773, 11, 476, 42286, 48765, 14212, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 701, 7290, 429, 807, 2225, 504, 1378, 2155, 18805, 13], "logp_list": [-0.0546, -0.0, -0.5958, -0.8335, -0.0235, -0.0064, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1576, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.9025, -0.1192, -0.0346, -0.0017, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.004, -0.2746, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.071, -0.0812, -0.0029, -0.0019, -0.0005, -0.0008, -0.0004, -0.0103, -0.0009, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.004, -0.0082, -0.1016, -0.0, -0.008, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.0011, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0