{"id": "608", "pred": "Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. Keep a master schedule for to make any changes. Microsoft Excel", "raw_output": "Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. Keep a master schedule for to make any changes. Microsoft Excel", "gt": "To do employee schedules, you need to first understand work laws related to overtime and age restrictions, and you may need to consult a lawyer for this. After that, make a list of all your employees and their duties. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create a chart of work days and hours for each day. Once the schedule is complete, it can be distributed to employees through printing physical copies or sending digital copies to employee email accounts. It's advisable to keep a master schedule in case changes need to be made. Tools like Microsoft Excel can be used to create these schedules, especially as your business grows.", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.361, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 53, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [8078, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 13, 7405, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 311, 1281, 894, 4344, 13, 5100, 21029], "logp_list": [-1.9307, -0.0039, -0.0499, -0.0042, -0.0922, -0.0254, -0.0009, -0.0052, -0.0048, -0.0001, -0.0031, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.8807, -0.1247, -