{"id": "614", "pred": "Step 2: Remove the printer from the devices list. Remove printers and uninstall any Windows print drivers using Windows Devices and Printers. If your printer connects to the computer with a USB cable, disconnect the cable from the printer. Turn the printer off and on again, and", "raw_output": "Step 2: Remove the printer from the devices list. Remove printers and uninstall any Windows print drivers using Windows Devices and Printers. If your printer connects to the computer with a USB cable, disconnect the cable from the printer. Turn the printer off and on again, and", "gt": "Based on the information given in the passages, to force remove a printer in devices and printers, you need to go to Control Panel, then click on Hardware and Sound, and then on Printers. Right-click the printer that you want to remove, and click Delete. If it doesn't delete, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete. If your printer is connected to your computer via a USB, disconnect the cable, turn the printer on and off again, and ensure it is in a ready state. If you used Print Manager or Printers folder to remove a printer or printer port, close these applications and stop and restart the Spooler Service.", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.869, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 55, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 17, 25, 10783, 279, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 13, 10783, 55953, 323, 53635, 894, 5515, 1173, 11788, 1667, 5515, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 13, 1416, 697, 22380, 33061, 311, 279, 6366, 448, 264, 11348, 14652, 11, 28969, 279, 14652, 504, 279, 22380, 13, 11999, 279, 22380, 1007, 323, 389, 1549, 11, 323], "logp_list": [-2.109, -0.0119, -0.569, -0.0206, -0.1613, -0.0118, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0017, -0.0016, -0.0002, -0.0236, -0.1362, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0081, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0017, -0.0061, -0.0015, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0075, -0.0947, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0017, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0092, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0013, -0.0002], "cumulative_logprob": -3.1887, "norm_logp": -0.058, "input_len": 263, "output_tokens": 55, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.73, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "620", "pred": "Technology has dramatically reshaped the average workplace in America over the", "raw_output": "Technology has dramatically reshaped the average workplace in America over the", "gt": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 2.508, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 12, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [62407, 702, 27957, 63693, 10185, 279, 5461, 26368, 304, 5159, 916, 279], "logp_list": [-0.4502, -0.0288, -0.2778, -0.0203, -0.0003, -0.0075, -0.007, -0.0003, -0.0312, -0.0101, -0.3326, -0.0009], "cumulative_logprob": -1.167, "norm_logp": -0.0972, "input_len": 251, "output_tokens": 12, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.21, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "629", "pred": "Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities", "raw_output": "Answer: Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some strategies for guarding a tall person in basketball:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard them near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities (Passage 1).\n2. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, to guard a tall person in basketball, it is important to stay close to them and create a barrier between them and the basket. These strategies can help limit their shooting opportunities and make it more difficult for them to score.", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.223, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 41, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 28737, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 264, 16217, 11, 25530, 31571, 979, 498, 7616, 1435, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 13, 3218, 3132, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488], "logp_list": [-0.8378, -0.0086, -0.3835, -0.1138, -0.0004, -0.0024, -0.0002, -0.0041, -0.0157, -0.001, -0.0196, -0.0001, -0.0012, -0.2426, -0.0033, -0.0024, -0.0052, -0.0015, -0.0004, -0.0015, -0.0043, -0.0001, -0.0369, -0.0162, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0058, -0.0036, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0051, -0.0004, -0.001, -0.0005], "cumulative_logprob": -1.7232, "norm_logp": -0.042, "input_len": 247, "output_tokens": 41, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.06, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "633", "pred": "Both the nervous system and endocrine system are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of of cells, tissues, organs, and systems. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs in the two systems.", "raw_output": "Both the nervous system and endocrine system are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of of cells, tissues, organs, and systems. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs in the two systems.", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system have both similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n1. Both systems are dedicated to maintaining homeostasis and coordinating the activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers play a crucial role in both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system occurs through electrochemical pulses, while chemical hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system utilizes interconnected cells to transmit signals, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals through neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.452, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 63, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [20629, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 315, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 11, 7892, 862, 1714, 315, 18368, 323, 4879, 43542, 304, 279, 1378, 5942, 13], "logp_list": [-0.755, -0.1754, -0.0089, -0.0432, -0.0002, -0.3936, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.1266, -0.0059, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0027, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0295, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.002, -0.0009, -0.0003, -0.0015, -0.4767, -0.0067, -0.0025, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0039, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.036, -0.5818, -0.0011, -0.0191, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.0023, -0.0197, -0.2849, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0015, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0022, -0.0273, -0.0039, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.1073, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0562], "cumulative_logprob": -3.1938, "norm_logp": -0.0507, "input_len": 278, "output_tokens": 63, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "637", "pred": "Pain-killing properties, spicy weight loss alternative, natural nasal decongestant, may help prevent heart disease, heart attack, and cancer, full of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants, cardiovascular health benefits.", "raw_output": "Pain-killing properties, spicy weight loss alternative, natural nasal decongestant, may help prevent heart disease, heart attack, and cancer, full of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants, cardiovascular health benefits.", "gt": "Jalapenos have numerous health benefits due to their capsaicin content. They have pain-killing properties and can serve as a natural nasal decongestant. They may also aid in weight loss and prevent heart disease, heart attacks, and possibly even cancer. Additionally, jalapenos are full of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants. They can also help increase cardiovascular health and defend heart health.", "question": "health benefits to jalapenos", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.838, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 43, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [47, 466, 12646, 9400, 5888, 11, 47251, 4680, 4709, 10555, 11, 5810, 71088, 409, 443, 6969, 517, 11, 1231, 1492, 5358, 4746, 8457, 11, 4746, 3359, 11, 323, 9387, 11, 2480, 315, 45092, 11, 32972, 11, 323, 80015, 11, 40613, 2820, 7567, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3666, -0.0011, -0.5008, -0.0007, -0.043, -0.0945, -0.3734, -0.0052, -0.0115, -0.021, -0.0034, -0.0772, -0.0035, -0.0018, -0.0008, -0.0037, -0.0011, -0.0061, -0.2757, -0.0921, -0.0109, -0.0062, -0.0035, -0.0498, -0.0709, -0.011, -0.0796, -0.0603, -0.5254, -0.0176, -0.0283, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0026, -0.0004, -0.0087, -0.0266, -0.0003, -0.3022, -1.0517, -0.0075, -0.2232, -0.3524], "cumulative_logprob": -5.7233, "norm_logp": -0.1331, "input_len": 279, "output_tokens": 43, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "641", "pred": "Similarities: - RBCs, WBCs are formed elements of blood. - RBCs, WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.", "raw_output": "Similarities: - RBCs, WBCs are formed elements of blood. - RBCs, WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.", "gt": "Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are found in the blood and are part of the circulatory system. They are both formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow and contain cell membranes and cytoplasm. The main difference is their functions. RBCs are responsible for delivering oxygen from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases, viruses, etc.", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 14.428, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 38, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 25, 481, 431, 4897, 82, 11, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 13, 481, 431, 4897, 82, 11, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 2518, 17240, 82648, 13], "logp_list": [-0.3817, -0.0019, -0.087, -0.1265, -0.2616, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0341, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0083, -0.002, -0.0161, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.0119, -0.0346, -0.003, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0244, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0092, -0.0036, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0011, -0.0011, -0.0006, -0.0721], "cumulative_logprob": -1.087, "norm_logp": -0.0286, "input_len": 405, "output_tokens": 38, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "646", "pred": "Cut large, sprouted potato into chunks with two or three eyes each, using a sharp knife, being careful to not break the long sprouts. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet, and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut end can dry out. Small potato can be planted whole. Water the potato thoroughly. Continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mul", "raw_output": "Answer: Cut large, sprouted potato into chunks with two or three eyes each, using a sharp knife, being careful to not break the long sprouts. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet, and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut end can dry out. Small potato can be planted whole. Water the potato thoroughly. Continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mul", "gt": "To plant a potato that has sprouted, follow these steps:\n\n1. Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each using a sharp knife.\n2. Set the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and allow them to dry out for a cool, dark location overnight.\n3. Once the cut ends are dry, thoroughly wash the potatoes.\n4. Plant the potatoes in the ground, either whole or cut into cubes with a sprout on each cube.\n5. Space the potatoes about 6 to 8 inches apart and cover them with a layer of compost.\n6. Replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\n7. Water the potatoes regularly when the soil is dry to the touch.\n8. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines.", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 22.934, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 114, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 19649, 3460, 11, 8151, 18533, 38734, 1119, 26757, 448, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 1817, 11, 1667, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 1660, 16585, 311, 537, 1438, 279, 1293, 8151, 11672, 13, 10771, 279, 38734, 26757, 389, 264, 34688, 476, 12544, 10834, 11, 323, 738, 1105, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 6319, 3728, 24398, 773, 279, 3931, 835, 646, 9058, 700, 13, 14994, 38734, 646, 387, 38341, 4361, 13, 9959, 279, 38734, 26364, 13, 15003, 72741, 15502, 979, 279, 17171, 374, 9058, 311, 279, 5796, 13, 2691, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 15602, 331, 2163, 279, 10779, 11, 22266, 432, 1182, 518, 3245, 220, 19, 14924, 504, 279, 8151, 10909, 38734, 85429, 13, 29351], "logp_list": [-1.0678, -0.0227, -0.5184, -0.4554, -0.0176, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0165, -0.0008, -0.0064, -0.0408, -0.0036, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0031, -0.0052, -0.0523, -0.0867, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0178, -0.0318, -0.0001, -0.0033, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0048, -0.0131, -0.0012, -0.0017, -0.0003, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.001, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0051, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.003, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0018, -0.0025, -0.044, -0.0184, -0.0015, -0.0038, -0.0037, -0.0007, -0.0243, -1.0503, -0.0151, -0.0271, -0.0069, -0.0051, -0.0087, -0.0008, -0.003, -0.0011, -0.0003, -0.001, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0018, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0017, -0.0168, -0.0013, -0.0012, -0.0007, -0.0105, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0017, -0.0002, -0.0017, -0.0007, -0.0015, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0031, -0.0009, -0.0025, -0.001, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0104, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0012, -0.0019, -0.0383], "cumulative_logprob": -3.7189, "norm_logp": -0.0326, "input_len": 542, "output_tokens": 114, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-