{"id": "650", "pred": "The color of urine can vary based on several factors, including the presence of blood, certain foods and medications, and kidney diseases. A normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this pale color of urine is sometimes altered when, in case of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunction function", "raw_output": "The color of urine can vary based on several factors, including the presence of blood, certain foods and medications, and kidney diseases. A normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this pale color of urine is sometimes altered when, in case of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunction function", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we know that red urine can indicate blood in the urine and can potentially be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. On the other hand, deep purple urine is associated with porphyria, a rare genetic disorder. The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome, but its color may change due to various factors such as kidney diseases. Therefore, the color of urine can provide important information about one's health and should be monitored closely.", "question": "color of urin meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 15.042, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 77, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 3118, 389, 3807, 9363, 11, 2670, 279, 9362, 315, 6543, 11, 3654, 15298, 323, 29910, 11, 323, 37942, 18808, 13, 362, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 419, 27539, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 7025, 28752, 979, 11, 304, 1142, 315, 37942, 18808, 11, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 525, 71187, 729], "logp_list": [-0.2917, -0.0261, -0.0022, -0.0233, -0.0528, -1.0328, -1.171, -0.0004, -0.6472, -0.0018, -0.886, -0.073, -0.5647, -0.0345, -0.0019, -0.1356, -0.266, -0.4401, -0.3125, -0.5159, -0.0035, -0.0171, -0.1814, -1.1767, -0.1835, -0.0602, -1.3676, -0.61, -0.5066, -0.5314, -0.0014, -0.0081, -0.0422, -0.0002, -0.5233, -0.7909, -0.0131, -0.019, -0.0001, -0.0098, -0.0003, -0.0038, -0.0, -0.0, -0.012, -0.1881, -0.0, -1.508, -0.1634, -0.0013, -0.0238, -0.0009, -0.1701, -0.0006, -0.0016, -0.0924, -0.106, -0.0008, -0.058, -0.0006, -0.0022, -0.0007, -0.0054, -0.0072, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0024, -0.0026, -0.0083, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0011, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.1744, -0.0032, -0.5051], "cumulative_logprob": -15.5745, "norm_logp": -0.2023, "input_len": 243, "output_tokens": 77, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "655", "pred": "Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion.", "raw_output": "Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Rinse your hair completely with warm water, then use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair (Passage 1, step 6).\n2. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type, and apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo into the palm of your hand while in the shower (Passage 2, steps 1-3). Work the shampoo through your hair without piling it up on your head, and avoid tangling it while it's still wet.\n3. After applying shampoo, rinse your hair thoroughly with warm water, and then comb through it with your fingers to remove any remaining tangles (Passage 1, step 7).\n4. Apply a conditioner to your hair, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes before rinsing it out with cool water (Passage 1, step 8).\n5. To dry your hair, gently pat it with a towel or wrap it around your head to absorb excess water, avoiding rubbing it vigorously with a towel (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide instructions on how to style or dry your hair after cleaning it.", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 15.855, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 81, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [49, 258, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 323, 11, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 990, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 13, 26530, 279, 64324, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 28337, 1137, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 13], "logp_list": [-1.5496, -0.0021, -0.0001, -0.1992, -0.0003, -0.0561, -0.7533, -0.1297, -0.0266, -0.0038, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0026, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0044, -0.002, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0014, -0.001, -0.0004, -0.0571, -0.3346, -0.0083, -0.0003, -0.007, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0055, -0.2239, -0.0098, -0.0001, -0.0093, -0.0048, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0209, -0.0019, -0.0004, -0.0008, -0.0007, -0.1846, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.0051, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0022, -0.0001, -0.0049, -0.0031, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0032, -0.0156, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0081], "cumulative_logprob": -3.6646, "norm_logp": -0.0452, "input_len": 406, "output_tokens": 81, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "662", "pred": "To use vinegar for dogs, you can mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse, spray vinegar full-strength on your dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin, make a rinse to improve your dog's skin and coat, clean out your dog's ears using ACv, spray your dog's coat to repel fleas, bathe in ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas, use a flea comb to remove the fleas, rinse your", "raw_output": "To use vinegar for dogs, you can mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse, spray vinegar full-strength on your dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin, make a rinse to improve your dog's skin and coat, clean out your dog's ears using ACv, spray your dog's coat to repel fleas, bathe in ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas, use a flea comb to remove the fleas, rinse your", "gt": "Sure, I can answer your question based on the given passages. Here are some uses for vinegar for dogs:\n\n1. Coat and skin health: Mixing vinegar with water and using it as a final rinse can help to rejuvenate your dog's coat and balance their skin pH levels, according to Passage 1.\n2. Flea control: Vinegar can be used to repel fleas and remove them from your dog's coat, as mentioned in Passage 2.\n3. Itchy ears: Diluted vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears, as stated in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions or if there's anything else I can assist you with.", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 21.033, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 106, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 990, 46105, 369, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 6514, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 323, 990, 438, 264, 1590, 73241, 11, 22899, 46105, 2480, 5477, 17842, 389, 697, 5562, 594, 22875, 311, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 1181, 6787, 11, 1281, 264, 73241, 311, 7269, 697, 5562, 594, 6787, 323, 22875, 11, 4240, 700, 697, 5562, 594, 24230, 1667, 10584, 85, 11, 22899, 697, 5562, 594, 22875, 311, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 11, 15743, 383, 304, 10584, 53, 33019, 391, 20980, 311, 4367, 12962, 300, 11, 990, 264, 95855, 3614, 311, 4057, 279, 12962, 300, 11, 73241, 697], "logp_list": [-1.4783, -0.7604, -0.073, -0.5647, -0.1004, -0.1617, -0.5452, -0.0918, -0.5219, -0.2192, -0.0026, -0.0601, -0.0076, -0.0033, -0.0028, -0.0016, -0.0026, -0.0603, -0.0447, -0.0008, -0.0019, -0.0003, -0.3172, -0.0381, -0.1741, -0.0012, -0.0022, -0.0005, -1.9909, -0.1034, -0.0616, -0.0264, -0.0542, -0.0012, -0.0091, -0.047, -0.0057, -0.0362, -0.0007, -0.0939, -0.0071, -0.0164, -0.0323, -0.1416, -0.0018, -0.0086, -0.0003, -0.0325, -0.7485, -0.0075, -0.0002, -0.0073, -0.0004, -0.0082, -0.0018, -0.0008, -0.0007, -0.0106, -0.0002, -0.0102, -0.0805, -0.0046, -0.0012, -0.0007, -0.0009, -0.0006, -0.0081, -0.162, -0.147, -0.0092, -0.0232, -0.0037, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.0002, -0.0011, -0.0022, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0083, -0.0545, -0.0001, -0.0114, -0.1943, -0.0409, -0.0074, -0.0006, -0.0008, -0.0037, -0.0018, -0.0908, -0.0001, -0.0157, -0.513, -0.0096, -0.0015, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.0036, -0.015, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0701, -0.5782, -0.0046], "cumulative_logprob": -10.7832, "norm_logp": -0.1017, "input_len": 318, "output_tokens": 106, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "666", "pred": "When you inhale, the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered and air is sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "raw_output": "When you inhale, the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered and air is sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "gt": "When you breathe in, your diaphragm contracts and pulls downwards, expanding the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also contract to expand the ribcage. Pressure inside the chest is reduced, causing air to be sucked into the lungs. On the other hand, when you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, reducing the space in the chest cavity. Air rich in carbon dioxide is then forced out of the lungs and windpipe. Breathing out does not require any effort from your body unless you have a lung disease or are doing physical activity.", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 24.193, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, 