{"id": "694", "pred": "No, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score.", "raw_output": "No, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that watching Snapchat stories does not directly increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is increased by sending and receiving more snaps, and by interacting with friends on the platform. Watching stories is not mentioned as a factor that contributes to increasing one's score. Therefore, the answer to the question is: No, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score.", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 2.412, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 11, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2753, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 697, 5456, 13], "logp_list": [-0.2769, -1.3173, -0.1314, -0.0041, -0.0054, -0.0334, -0.0006, -0.0332, -0.7103, -0.3147, -0.0296], "cumulative_logprob": -2.8569, "norm_logp": -0.2597, "input_len": 416, "output_tokens": 11, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.73, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "698", "pred": "Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen,", "raw_output": "Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen,", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\nPassage 1 provides instructions for making ice cream using an ice cream maker. To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes). Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nPassage 2 provides a recipe for making ice cream from scratch. To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Then, heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n\nPassage 3 provides general instructions for making ice cream bases. To make ice cream, you will need to start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This type of base is made with cream rather than custard, and it results in a lighter and less icy texture. To make one quart of ice cream, you will need to double the recipe.\n\nTherefore, to summarize:\n\nTo make ice cream using an ice cream maker:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker and turn on the machine.\n2. Churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes).\n3. Serve the ice cream immediately or place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nTo make ice cream from scratch:\n\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges.\n3. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract.\n4. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.521, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 63, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [42178, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 11, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 11, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 13963, 594, 17961, 11, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 3197, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 304, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 11, 220], "logp_list": [-1.0913, -0.1665, -0.0016, -0.0013, -0.0018, -0.002, -0.0066, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0023, -0.0972, -0.0202, -0.0022, -0.0009, -0.003, -0.0156, -0.0072, -0.0001, -0.0132, -0.0008, -0.0179, -0.0078, -0.0112, -0.1224, -0.0137, -0.0046, -0.0003, -0.0028, -0.0004, -0.0019, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.0255, -0.401, -0.0137, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0017, -0.0014, -0.0028, -0.0031, -0.0004, -0.0024, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0009, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0012, -0.0004, -0.0021, -0.0087, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0522, -0.0047], "cumulative_logprob": -2.1459, "norm_logp": -0.0341, "input_len": 291, "output_tokens": 63, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.94, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "705", "pred": "children learn about floating and sinking and seeing that different objects can sink and float.", "raw_output": "children learn about floating and sinking and seeing that different objects can sink and float.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 3.338, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 16, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [5864, 3960, 911, 19057, 323, 61093, 323, 9120, 429, 2155, 6171, 646, 19309, 323, 2224, 13], "logp_list": [-0.4061, -0.3512, -0.6909, -0.3525, -0.0635, -0.0083, -1.1559, -0.0948, -0.0258, -0.0049, -0.0047, -0.0021, -0.0029, -0.0059, -0.0033, -0.9507], "cumulative_logprob": -4.1235, "norm_logp": -0.2577, "input_len": 371, "output_tokens": 16, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
