{"id": "728", "pred": "The Wellesley forecast for August 22 is 82 degrees and Sunny with a 39 percentage chance of rain and 10 mph winds from the North-Northwest.", "raw_output": "Answer: The Wellesley forecast for August 22 is 82 degrees and Sunny with a 39 percentage chance of rain and 10 mph winds from the North-Northwest.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the weather in Wellesley for Tuesday, August 23rd is expected to be sunny with a high of 82 degrees and a 39% chance of rain. The wind speed is expected to be 10 mph from the north-northwest.", "question": "weather in wellesley", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 9.187, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 41, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 576, 25006, 642, 3179, 17595, 369, 6156, 220, 17, 17, 374, 220, 23, 17, 12348, 323, 55038, 448, 264, 220, 18, 24, 11414, 6012, 315, 11174, 323, 220, 16, 15, 33961, 28492, 504, 279, 4787, 11250, 2364, 11039, 13], "logp_list": [-1.2574, -0.1471, -0.8276, -0.8774, -0.0006, -0.0012, -0.26, -0.2515, -0.2844, -0.0869, -0.1137, -0.2213, -0.371, -0.0795, -0.1435, -0.0093, -0.0005, -0.0936, -0.1279, -0.86, -0.0712, -0.0074, -0.0096, -0.0856, -0.2533, -0.0013, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0249, -0.0072, -0.0045, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0029, -0.0011, -0.0024, -0.0005, -0.0041, -0.0, -0.0535], "cumulative_logprob": -6.5449, "norm_logp": -0.1596, "input_len": 325, "output_tokens": 41, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "733", "pred": "The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air. This exchange happens in the lungs", "raw_output": "The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air. This exchange happens in the lungs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how the air you breathe is processed before it reaches your lungs:\n\nWhen you inhale, the diaphragm muscle contracts, moving down from the bottom of your rib cage towards your abdominal region, which causes the thoracic cavity to increase in volume. This decrease in air pressure in the lungs below atmospheric pressure forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing you to inhale.\n\nTherefore, the air you breathe is processed by the diaphragm muscle before it reaches your lungs, which contracts to take air into the lungs and relax to let it out again. Additionally, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, such as oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment, which occurs in the lungs.", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 9.191, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 46, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 429, 13666, 1948, 498, 11, 304, 3953, 11, 279, 7761, 315, 697, 2487, 11, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 11, 892, 374, 279, 3720, 13, 1096, 9289, 8573, 304, 279, 44174], "logp_list": [-0.2909, -0.3329, -0.1826, -0.2055, -0.0999, -0.0475, -0.0368, -0.0002, -0.0027, -0.0812, -0.08, -0.2831, -0.0153, -0.0037, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.505, -0.0069, -0.0004, -0.1588, -0.0112, -0.006, -0.0021, -0.0017, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0004, -0.0038, -0.0057, -0.0011, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0013, -0.0066, -0.0076, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0061, -0.3289, -0.0006, -0.0006, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -2.723, "norm_logp": -0.0592, "input_len": 364, "output_tokens": 46, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.48, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "739", "pred": "SMS stands for Short Message Service and is also commonly referred to as a text message. With a SMS, you can send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will automatically be split by into several parts. Most cell phones support this type of text messaging. MMS: MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and this type of text messaging is an evolution of the SMS. With a MMS, you can send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. It is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone", "raw_output": "SMS stands for Short Message Service and is also commonly referred to as a text message. With a SMS, you can send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will automatically be split by into several parts. Most cell phones support this type of text messaging. MMS: MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and this type of text messaging is an evolution of the SMS. With a MMS, you can send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. It is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone", "gt": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the given passages:\n\nThe main difference between SMS (Short Message Service) and MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is that SMS is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows for sending multimedia content such as images, videos, and audio files, in addition to text.\n\nAccording to passage 1, SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts if they are longer. MMS messages, on the other hand, can carry a larger size of content, including pictures, videos, and audio files, with a maximum size of 300KB.\n\nPassage 2 explains that SMS is a premium service offered by mobile companies, while passage 3 highlights the differences between SMS and MMS, stating that SMS only allows for text, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between SMS and MMS are:\n\n* SMS is limited to text-only messages, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n* SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts, while MMS messages can carry a larger size of content.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 23.981, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 121, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [65565, 13352, 369, 10698, 4856, 5362, 323, 374, 1083, 16626, 13862, 311, 438, 264, 1467, 1943, 13, 3085, 264, 29909, 11, 498, 646, 3624, 264, 1943, 315, 705, 311, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 311, 2441, 3671, 13, 93326, 6605, 686, 9463, 387, 6718, 553, 1119, 3807, 5479, 13, 7496, 2779, 17619, 1824, 419, 943, 315, 1467, 29522, 13, 386, 4826, 25, 386, 4826, 13352, 369, 82222, 73170, 5362, 323, 419, 943, 315, 1467, 29522, 374, 458, 15379, 315, 279, 29909, 13, 3085, 264, 386, 4826, 11, 498, 646, 3624, 264, 1943, 2670, 9185, 11, 2766, 11, 476, 7699, 2213, 311, 2441, 3671, 13, 1084, 374, 1429, 16626, 1483, 311, 3624, 264, 6548, 4429, 448, 264, 6249, 4540, 311, 2441, 4540], "logp_list": [-0.9848, -0.8677, -0.0012, -0.0231, -0.0034, -0.0009, -0.2481, -0.2346, -0.3142, -0.0023, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0115, -0.0005, -0.0015, -0.0354, -0.7372, -0.0031, -0.0014, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.049, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0553, -0.0134, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0014, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0063, -0.0317, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0027, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.404, -0.0119, -0.001, -0.0007, -0.3714, -0.2195, -0.0009, -0.0015, -0.0003, -0.0076, -0.0016, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.1394, -0.0954, -0.0002, -0.0344, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0013, -0.0002, -0.007, -0.0262, -0.0376, -0.0012, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0008, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0071, -0.0131, -0.1364, -0.0024, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0017, -0.0001, -0.0019, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0012, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0027, -0.0016, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0015, -0.0012, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0044, -0.1164, -0.0015, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0007, -0.0009, -0.0007, -0.0036], "cumulative_logprob": -5.3225, "norm_logp": -0.044, "input_len": 471, "output_tokens": 121, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "21", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. The", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. The", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services. They administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. The site is also for providers, offering them resources like weekly Q&A sessions each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. where they can address their questions and issues. Additionally, they offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses, approved by organizations like the American Psychological Association and the Association of Social Work Boards.", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 191.344, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 26, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 18432, 264, 17059, 1618, 1817, 6602, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 481, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 576], "logp_list": [-0.1184, -0.0005, -0.0853, -0.0002, -2.4595, -0.2441, -0.002, -0.0353, -0.0432, -0.0002, -0.0127, -0.0007, -0.0006, -0.0439, -0.0014, -0.0283, -0.1315, -0.0014, -0.0003, -0.0037, -0.1351, -0.2217, -0.0046, -0.0003, -0.0239, -0.424], "cumulative_logprob": -4.0228, "norm_logp": -0.1547, "input_len": 319, "output_tokens": 26, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "27", "pred": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry on the jamb until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from it's original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "raw_output": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry on the jamb until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from it's original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 1781.225, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 2, "n_tokens": 139, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 432, 594, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13], "logp_list": [-2.1908, -0.0041, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.0078, -0.0058, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0216, -0.0461, -0.0049, -0.0107, -0.0706, -0.0023, -0.2896, -0.03, -0.0062, -0.0001, -0.4524, -0.0453, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0064, -0.0441, -0.0152, -0.0043, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0033, -0.0016, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0416, -0.0055, -0.7497, -0.1196, -1.1651, -0.0003, -0.2099, -0.1528, -0.0153, -0.0024, -0.1529, -0.0148, -0.0908, -0.0162, -0.01, -0.0271, -0.033, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0022, -0.0006, -0.0073, -0.0026, -0.0104, -0.0792, -0.0519, -0.0003, -0.6003, -0.2231, -0.0114, -0.0039, -0.0234, -0.0044, -0.0074, -0.0339, -0.0019, -0.0008, -0.0233, -0.009, -0.0085, -0.0019, -0.0277, -0.0029, -0.0022, -0.0023, -0.0045, -0.0016, -0.7059, -0.0107, -0.0018, -0.0048, -0.0049, -0.2475, -0.0085, -0.0022, -0.0004, -0.0227, -0.0002, -0.0021, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.0038, -0.0029, -0.071, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0059, -0.0017, -0.0085, -0.0038, -0.0028, -0.0016, -0.0363, -0.0095, -0.0026, -0.0009, -0.0005, -0.004, -0.0071, -0.0042, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0059, -0.0007, -0.008, -0.0039, -0.0004, -0.0016, -0.007, -0.1019, -0.0004, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0034, -0.0014, -0.0004, -0.0108, -0.0323], "cumulative_logprob": -8.5939, "norm_logp": -0.0618, "input_len": 511, "output_tokens": 139, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "32", "pred": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry on the jamb until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from it's original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "raw_output": "Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry on the jamb until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from it's original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a possible solution to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check if the door stops are properly aligned. If the door stops are not aligned, use a chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose. Remove the door stop and use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb and set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n2. Check if the latch hole in the jamb is properly aligned with the strike plate. If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, tighten the hinges first. Then, enlarge the strike plate hole. Move the strike plate if necessary.\n\nIf these steps do not solve the problem, it may be necessary to seek further assistance from a professional locksmith or carpenter.", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 46.414, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 2, "n_tokens": 139, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 432, 594, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13], "logp_list": [-2.1908, -0.0041, -0.0024, -0.0001, -0.0078, -0.0058, -0.0008, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0216, -0.0461, -0.0049, -0.0107, -0.0706, -0.0023, -0.2896, -0.03, -0.0062, -0.0001, -0.4524, -0.0453, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0064, -0.0441, -0.0152, -0.0043, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0033, -0.0016, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.0416, -0.0055, -0.7497, -0.1196, -1.1651, -0.0003, -0.2099, -0.1528, -0.0153, -0.0024, -0.1529, -0.0148, -0.0908, -0.0162, -0.01, -0.0271, -0.033, -0.0001, -0.0014, -0.0022, -0.0006, -0.0073, -0.0026, -0.0104, -0.0792, -0.0519, -0.0003, -0.6003, -0.2231, -0.0114, -0.0039, -0.0234, -0.0044, -0.0074, -0.0339, -0.0019, -0.0008, -0.0233, -0.009, -0.0085, -0.0019, -0.0277, -0.0029, -0.0022, -0.0023, -0.0045, -0.0016, -0.7059, -0.0107, -0.0018, -0.0048, -0.0049, -0.2475, -0.0085, -0.0022, -0.0004, -0.0227, -0.0002, -0.0021, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.0038, -0.0029, -0.071, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0059, -0.0017, -0.0085, -0.0038, -0.0028, -0.0016, -0.0363, -0.0095, -0.0026, -0.0009, -0.0005, -0.004, -0.0071, -0.0042, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0059, -0.0007, -0.008, -0.0039, -0.0004, -0.0016, -0.007, -0.1019, -0.0004, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0034, -0.0014, -0.0004, -0.0108, -0.0323], "cumulative_logprob": -8.5939, "norm_logp": -0.0618, "input_len": 511, "output_tokens": 139, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "36", "pred": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees f (175 degrees c). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off", "raw_output": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees f (175 degrees c). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn oven off", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook pollock:\n\nPassage 1:\n\n* Spray a baking sheet with butter-flavored cooking spray.\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Place the fillets on the baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n* Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 2:\n\n* Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Bake the fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n* Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n* Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on top of each fillet.\n* Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.\n\nTherefore, to cook pollock, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n2. Place the fillets on a baking sheet or in the oven.\n3. Cook the pollock until it flakes easily, either by baking it in the oven or on the stovetop.\n4. Add cheese to the pollock if desired and return it to the oven to melt the cheese.", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.506, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 53, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 282, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 272, 568, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 13, 52074, 304, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 11999, 23387, 1007], "logp_list": [-0.9853, -0.0022, -0.3049, -0.0235, -0.0138, -0.2225, -0.0016, -0.0008, -0.0087, -0.1057, -0.0619, -0.002, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0089, -0.1674, -0.2041, -0.0547, -0.0035, -0.0004, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0005, -0.0006, -0.0157, -0.0284, -0.0067, -0.0075, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0114, -0.0053, -0.169, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.0001, -0.0044, -0.0016, -0.0011, -0.0027, -0.0003, -0.0047, -0.0047, -0.1504, -0.0283, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -2.6237, "norm_logp": -0.0495, "input_len": 267, "output_tokens": 53, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "40", "pred": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "raw_output": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in in solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first, run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Next, apply nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth and then mix liquid laundry soap with water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 24.472, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 120, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [6727, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 