{"id": "54", "pred": "Benefits of a Water Pik include helping to maintain good oral health by massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and cleaning better around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas area that brushing can not access.", "raw_output": "Benefits of a Water Pik include helping to maintain good oral health by massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and cleaning better around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas area that brushing can not access.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the benefits of a water pick include:\n\n* Helping to keep teeth, gums, mouth, and overall body healthier by eliminating pesky germs and plaque that are difficult to remove with a toothbrush.\n* Massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth to reduce the risk of gingivitis.\n* Cleaning better around the teeth and gums, removing food particles from areas that brushing cannot access.\n\nTherefore, using a water pick can be an effective addition to your oral hygiene routine, complementing traditional brushing and flossing methods.", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 10.36, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 51, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [84323, 315, 264, 9959, 61162, 2924, 10476, 311, 10306, 1661, 20655, 2820, 553, 3072, 4118, 323, 64692, 8413, 19847, 304, 279, 10780, 11, 17719, 279, 5214, 315, 66093, 344, 19435, 11, 323, 15826, 2664, 2163, 279, 17832, 323, 97654, 11, 17592, 3607, 504, 5671, 3082, 429, 76726, 646, 537, 2615, 13], "logp_list": [-0.957, -0.0222, -0.0504, -0.6937, -0.0923, -0.1737, -1.2009, -0.0543, -0.1234, -0.0105, -0.0006, -0.0071, -0.9985, -0.0459, -0.0001, -0.0013, -0.0021, -0.0145, -0.0077, -0.0879, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.1508, -0.3905, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0561, -0.0151, -0.0016, -0.0102, -0.0629, -0.0546, -0.5864, -0.0069, -0.0183, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.3838, -0.0056, -0.7797, -0.0236, -0.4799, -0.3745, -0.0033, -0.0545, -0.1567, -0.0039, -0.0033, -0.018], "cumulative_logprob": -8.1859, "norm_logp": -0.1605, "input_len": 317, "output_tokens": 51, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "59", "pred": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. The netting keep the birds from reaching those spaces they often", "raw_output": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. The netting keep the birds from reaching those spaces they often", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun (Passage 1:4). This will prevent birds from reaching the areas they often choose to build their nests.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it (Passage 2:1). Choose a non-flammable netting that is safe to use around light bulbs, and ensure that it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds from the area (Passage 3:1). Move the plastic hawk periodically to avoid the birds becoming accustomed to it.\n\nPlease note that the effectiveness of these methods may vary depending on the type of birds and the location of your porch. If the above methods do not work, you may need to consider other solutions or consult with a professional for assistance.", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 11.672, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 55, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [30485, 11958, 4179, 1280, 311, 279, 384, 2342, 2163, 279, 46342, 315, 697, 44647, 448, 264, 48956, 6038, 13, 1416, 697, 44647, 702, 1787, 52455, 388, 11, 990, 279, 48956, 6038, 311, 15498, 279, 4179, 1280, 311, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 44647, 13, 576, 4179, 1280, 2506, 279, 19654, 504, 18739, 1846, 12621, 807, 3545], "logp_list": [-0.3129, -0.29, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0616, -0.0084, -0.0129, -0.0011, -0.0539, -0.0083, -0.0041, -0.0039, -0.0122, -0.0001, -0.0939, -0.0006, -0.0012, -0.002, -0.2395, -0.8537, -0.0052, -0.0006, -0.0546, -0.0146, -0.0007, -0.0009, -0.0014, -0.0004, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0112, -0.3131, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.1984, -0.0015, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0008, -0.0004, -0.0011, -0.0019], "cumulative_logprob": -2.5741, "norm_logp": -0.0468, "input_len": 422, "output_tokens": 55, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.21, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "64", "pred": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag", "raw_output": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag", "gt": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is either by separating the blue field from the flag and burning it in a peaceful manner before burying the ashes, or by conducting a proper ceremony where the flag is folded in the customary triangle fold and then burned.", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 2.268, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 10, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181], "logp_list": [-0.8823, -0.0292, -0.0072, -0.0018, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0024, -0.0004, -0.3738, -0.0009], "cumulative_logprob": -1.2988, "norm_logp": -0.1299, "input_len": 246, "output_tokens": 10, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "73", "pred": "Avoid physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling. If the guy you're flirting with seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so. Don't", "raw_output": "Avoid physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling. If the guy you're flirting with seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so. Don't", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you:\n\n1. Physical contact: Avoid physical contact that could be misinterpreted as fondling or sexual activity (Passage 1).\n2. Eye contact: If your coworker is consistently staring at you, it may be a sign that they are interested in you (Passage 2).\n3. Smiling: If your coworker smiles at you excessively, even when there is no apparent reason to do so, it may be a sign of flirtation (Passage 2).\n4. Seeking contact: If your coworker consistently finds reasons to be near you or seek you out discreetly, it may indicate that they have feelings for you (Passage 3).\n\nHowever, it is essential to remember that these signs alone do not necessarily mean that your coworker is interested in you romantically. It's important to pay attention to the context of their behavior and communicate openly to avoid misunderstandings.\n\nIf you are unsure about your coworker's intentions, it may be best to avoid physical contact and observe their behavior over time before making any conclusions. Additionally, it's crucial to respect your coworker's boundaries and maintain a professional work environment.", "question": "how to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.843, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 43, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [52116, 6961, 3645,