{"id": "235", "pred": "The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by an annual precipitation of 34 inches, with an average of 256 sunny days per year. The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees, while the lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees. The", "raw_output": "The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by an annual precipitation of 34 inches, with an average of 256 sunny days per year. The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees, while the lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees. The", "gt": "Average weather in Sausalito can vary depending on the time of year. For example, during September, the average temperature is 58 degrees Fahrenheit (15 degrees Celsius), while in January, it is only 43 degrees Fahrenheit (4 degrees Celsius). The most precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches. However, throughout the year, the number of days with measurable precipitation is 56, and there are an average of 256 sunny days.", "question": "average weather sausalito", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.101, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 60, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 31871, 553, 458, 9775, 59950, 315, 220, 18, 19, 14924, 11, 448, 458, 5461, 315, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 13, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6122, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 11, 1393, 279, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6652, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 13, 576], "logp_list": [-0.8445, -0.1514, -0.3684, -0.07, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0001, -1.1775, -0.4311, -0.0145, -1.0855, -0.6424, -0.2925, -0.0137, -0.0087, -0.0206, -0.065, -0.0027, -0.0818, -0.4838, -1.3566, -0.1006, -0.6425, -0.0053, -0.3536, -0.1888, -0.0073, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.0543, -0.0001, -0.1406, -0.1341, -0.7461, -0.2903, -0.0217, -0.0021, -0.7097, -0.2266, -0.0183, -0.022, -0.0059, -0.0038, -0.0003, -0.014, -0.1902, -0.0048, -0.0025, -0.1715, -0.0005, -0.0041, -0.3212, -0.0044, -0.0126, -0.0003, -0.0057, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.6645], "cumulative_logprob": -12.1849, "norm_logp": -0.2031, "input_len": 429, "output_tokens": 60, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "243", "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps or pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out.", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps or pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are large square structures made of wire or flat metal mesh, with two ends that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. Crabs are attracted to bait inside the pot and must crawl up the leads to reach it, but once they enter, they cannot escape due to the narrow opening. The pot is designed to allow crabs in but not let them out, making it an effective tool for catching crabs.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How do crab traps work?\" is: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage with a narrow entrance that allows crabs to enter but not exit, making it an effective tool for catching crabs.", "question": "how do crab traps work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 9.325, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 46, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [16001, 370, 44560, 975, 553, 1667, 264, 1849, 315, 52457, 4766, 264, 3460, 9317, 35360, 1865, 315, 9067, 476, 10063, 9317, 11294, 429, 374, 48580, 448, 9509, 15904, 13, 576, 44560, 476, 50031, 525, 6188, 311, 2138, 1560, 3435, 304, 714, 537, 1077, 1105, 700, 13], "logp_list": [-0.3833, -0.0005, -0.0615, -0.3189, -0.0738, -0.1634, -0.0418, -0.035, -0.0019, -0.0011, -0.01, -0.0066, -0.0069, -0.0058, -0.0003, -0.1865, -0.004, -0.0012, -0.00