{"id": "248", "pred": "The difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like", "raw_output": "The difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.847, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 45, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 279, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 19853, 279, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 11, 323, 432, 3171, 1405, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 1075], "logp_list": [-1.3182, -0.8005, -0.0169, -0.4456, -0.0004, -0.1145, -0.0574, -0.1809, -0.0329, -0.7643, -0.1017, -0.0341, -0.015, -0.2216, -0.0129, -0.0103, -0.0056, -0.0012, -0.0016, -0.0424, -0.0216, -0.0026, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0011, -0.0367, -0.0292, -0.0144, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0148, -0.0015, -0.0011, -0.038, -0.0055, -0.0019, -0.0007, -0.5937, -0.0043, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0012, -0.0012, -0.0186], "cumulative_logprob": -4.9687, "norm_logp": -0.1104, "input_len": 266, "output_tokens": 45, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "252", "pred": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavor flavor until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops that indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "raw_output": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavor flavor until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops that indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. (Passage 1)\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. (Passage 1)\n3. For Oven-Fried Pork Chops, use stuffing mix for the breading. The pork chops come out tender and juicy. This recipe takes 30 minutes to prepare and 10 minutes to prep. (Passage 2)\n4. To grill pork chops over indirect heat, rinse the chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat for 10 minutes before grilling. Grill the chops until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com, you should preheat the grill, season the pork chops with a spice mixture, and grill them over indirect heat until they are cooked through.", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 22.145, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 109, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 3786, 279, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 17172, 3080, 26364, 10856, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 11, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 26, 2138, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 429, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13], "logp_list": [-0.7998, -0.0018, -0.2734, -0.0024, -0.0002, -0.0154, -0.0009, -0.0028, -0.0479, -0.0373, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0017, -0.029, -0.1725, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0033, -0.0018, -0.0438, -0.1641, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.0007, -0.0007, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0021, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.004, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0027, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0015, -0.0036, -0.0027, -0.0303, -0.0083, -0.2317, -0.0126, -0.002, -0.0006, -0.0065, -0.0034, -0.0, -0.0015, -0.0001, -0.004, -0.0003, -0.001, -0.0014, -0.0048, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0043, -0.0524, -0.5452, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.0014, -0.0011, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0008, -0.0095, -0.0016, -0.0011, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0291, -0.0034, -0.2744, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.3889, -0.0024, -0.0004, -0.0017, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0003, -0.0033, -0.0034, -0.0006, -0.0011, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.002, -0.1045, -0.0026, -0.0273], "cumulative_logprob": -3.4008, "norm_logp": -0.0312, "input_len": 277, "output_tokens": 109, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "259", "pred": "To clean your dryer vent, remove the outside cover on the vent, and use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.", "raw_output": "To clean your dryer vent, remove the outside cover on the vent, and use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean dryer vent\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo clean the dryer vent, start by locating the vent cover on the outside of the house and removing it. Then, remove the vent from the back of the dryer and use a dryer vent brush to clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning the area around the lint filter for a more thorough cleaning. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits and ensure your dryer runs efficiently.\n\nIf the passages did not contain the necessary information to answer the question, I would have replied with \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.633, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 33, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 697, 46622, 10378, 11, 4057, 279, 4889, 3421, 389, 279, 10378, 11, 323, 990, 264, 3281, 57920, 15625, 448, 458, 13036, 480, 3705, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 13647, 13], "logp_list": [-0.5767, -0.0025, -0.6985, -0.0022, -0.0011, -0.0187, -0.4791, -0.0002, -0.0071, -0.0132, -0.0084, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.1279, -0.0236, -0.0082, -0.0008, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0013, -0.0005, -0.0012, -0.0005, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0081], "cumulative_logprob": -1.9858, "norm_logp": -0.0602, "inpu