{"id": "265", "pred": "MSM powder benefits the body by helping to get oxygen into the blood a lot more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels, helping to absorb more nutrients (vitamins and minerals), relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "raw_output": "MSM powder benefits the body by helping to get oxygen into the blood a lot more efficiently with the same amount of work, increasing energy levels, helping to absorb more nutrients (vitamins and minerals), relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the benefits of MSM powder include:\n\n* Helping to increase oxygen efficiency in the blood\n* Increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable\n* Enhancing nutrient absorption, particularly when taken with Co-enzyme Q10\n* Relieving muscular aches and pains\n* Reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis\n\nTherefore, MSM powder has several benefits for overall health and wellness, including improved oxygenation, energy, and reduction of pain and inflammation.", "question": "the benefits of msm powder", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 12.356, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 61, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4826, 44, 16723, 7567, 279, 2487, 553, 10476, 311, 633, 23552, 1119, 279, 6543, 264, 2696, 803, 29720, 448, 279, 1852, 3311, 315, 975, 11, 7703, 4802, 5866, 11, 10476, 311, 34306, 803, 36393, 320, 54811, 37825, 323, 32972, 701, 58544, 4405, 51092, 264, 8528, 323, 50166, 11, 323, 17719, 36040, 4152, 311, 10895, 476, 46188, 18808, 1741, 438, 54552, 13], "logp_list": [-1.3569, -0.0003, -0.3481, -0.5603, -0.1942, -0.0039, -0.3897, -0.2007, -0.0513, -0.062, -0.0154, -0.0013, -0.0017, -0.0017, -0.6034, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0536, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.3085, -0.3628, -0.0044, -0.3321, -0.5897, -0.3749, -0.915, -0.158, -0.0114, -0.0018, -0.6025, -0.0085, -0.0183, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.071, -1.002, -0.0002, -0.0041, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0033, -0.0008, -0.0162, -0.0705, -0.0026, -0.0018, -0.0317, -0.0, -0.0018, -0.0037, -0.0007, -0.0004, -0.042, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.0507], "cumulative_logprob": -8.8392, "norm_logp": -0.1449, "input_len": 242, "output_tokens": 61, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "276", "pred": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition that virtually no symptoms until severe bone damage has already occurred. Once the bones have been weakened by bone density loss, symptoms may include: 1  Back pain.2  Loss of height over time with stooped posture. 3  Fractures of the vertebrae, wrists,", "raw_output": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition that virtually no symptoms until severe bone damage has already occurred. Once the bones have been weakened by bone density loss, symptoms may include: 1  Back pain.2  Loss of height over time with stooped posture. 3  Fractures of the vertebrae, wrists,", "gt": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition characterized by significant bone density loss, resulting in weakened bones and increased risk of fractures. Symptoms may include sudden and severe back pain, loss of height over time, fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, fractures, particularly in the spine or hips, are likely to occur.", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 13.432, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 67, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1514, 19289, 51268, 88666, 10704, 374, 264, 2971, 429, 21214, 902, 13495, 3080, 15386, 17240, 5557, 702, 2669, 10017, 13, 9646, 279, 24854, 614, 1012, 57664, 553, 17240, 17457, 4709, 11, 13495, 1231, 2924, 25, 220, 16, 220, 6841, 6646, 13, 17, 220, 24704, 315, 2608, 916, 882, 448, 42032, 16367, 47278, 13, 220, 18, 220, 2869, 531, 1413, 315, 279, 5198, 50213, 68, 11, 85778, 11], "logp_list": [-0.4546, -0.0003, -0.0059, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.8968, -1.1135, -0.0109, -0.8744, -0.9025, -0.1524, -0.0012, -0.0264, -0.024, -0.0027, -0.0043, -0.3608, -0.0198, -0.0009, -0.0204, -0.9922, -0.001, -0.0013, -0.0027, -0.0024, -0.0009, -0.0021, -0.0015, -0.0009, -0.0021, -0.0429, -0.0109, -0.0045, -0.0022, -0.1969, -0.2691, -0.0063, -0.6287, -0.0171, -0.0005, -0.0263, -0.1728, -0.0076, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.4116, -0.0186, -0.0009, -0.0035, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0016, -0.1337, -0.1884, -0.1076, -0.0018, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0022, -0.0006, -0.0001], "cumulative_logprob": -8.1387, "norm_logp": -0.1215, "input_len": 500, "output_tokens": 67, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "283", "pred": "An adverb clause is a dependent clause that modifies a verb, adjective or another adverb. It usually modifies the verb. Adverb clauses are introduced by subordinate conjunctions including after, although, as, as if, before, because, so, since, so that, than, though, unless, until. An adjective clause is a dependent clause that modifies a noun or a pronoun. It will begin with a relative pronoun (who, whose, whom, which, and that) or a subordinate conjunction (when and where.", "raw_output": "An adverb clause is a dependent clause that modifies a verb, adjective or another adverb. It usually modifies the verb. Adverb clauses are introduced by subordinate conjunctions including after, although, as, as if, before, because, so, since, so that, than, though, unless, until. An adjective clause is a dependent clause that modifies a noun or a pronoun. It will begin with a relative pronoun (who, whose, whom, which, and that) or a subordinate conjunction (when and where.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, an adverb clause modifies a verb, adjective or another adverb, while an adjective clause modifies a noun or pronoun.", "question": "difference between an adverb clause and an adjective clause", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 21.84, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 108, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [2082, 993, 22328, 21647, 374, 264, 17749, 21647, 429, 82949, 264, 18607, 11, 84492, 476, 2441, 993, 22328, 13, 1084, 5990, 82949, 279, 18607, 13, 2410, 22328, 49098, 525, 11523, 553, 78163, 31446, 82, 2670, 1283, 11, 7892, 11, 438, 11, 438, 421, 11, 1573, 11, 1576, 11, 773, 11, 2474, 11, 773, 429, 11, 1091, 11, 3498, 11, 7241, 11, 3080, 13, 1527, 84492, 21647, 374, 264, 17749, 21647, 429, 82949, 264, 36921, 476, 264, 18613, 1624, 13, 1084, 686, 3161, 448, 264, 8674, 18613, 1624, 320, 14623, 11, 6693, 11, 8711, 11, 892, 11, 323, 429, 8, 476, 264, 78163, 31446, 320, 9309, 323, 1380, 13], "logp_list": [-0.3746, -0.0253, -0.0007, -0.0249, -0.6092, -0.0332, -0.0118, -0.0003, -0.0079, -0.0054, -0.0103, -0.0008, -0.0047, -0.0115, -0.8982, -0.0199, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.7374, -0.3041, -0.0333, -0.0017, -0.013, -0.0002, -0.1431, -0.3186, -0.004, -0.003, -0.0247, -0.0893, -0.0046, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0452, -0.0022, -0.0003, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0003, -0.0004, -0.0347, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -1.039, -0.048, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0001, -0.0019, -0.0001, -0.0013, -0.0006, -0.0112, -0.4084, -0.6982, -0.0125, -0.0025, -0.0493, -0.5205, -0.0085, -0.0013, -0.0228, -0.205, -0.0149, -0.0003, -0.0051, -0.0895, -0.0003, -0.0017, -0.0121, -0.4451, -0.0439, -0.012, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0739, -0.0041, -0.0002, -0.0014, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.0029, -0.0155, -0.0088, -0.0061, -0.0646, -0.0042, -0.0011, -0.0024, -0.0004, -0.0355, -0.0097, -0.133, -0.0048, -0.1457], "cumulative_logprob": -7.9785, "norm_logp": -0.0739, "input_len": 276, "output_tokens": 108, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "290", "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.Next, cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking.When internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for  30 minutes before serving.", "raw_output": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.Next, cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking.When internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for  30 minutes before serving.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Defrost the pork loin if possible. If you don't have time to defrost, you can place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour.\n2. Preheat the oven to 325°F (passage 2).\n3. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with 2 tsp of olive oil and season the outside with salt, pepper, and desired herbs (thyme, oregano, or garlic work well) (passage 2).\n4. Place the pork loin in a roasting pan and put it in the preheated oven (passage 2).\n5. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound, or until the internal temperature reaches 150°F (passage 3).\n6. Use a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature of the meat (passage 3).\n7. Once the meat is cooked, remove it from the oven and cover it with aluminum foil for 30 minutes before serving (passage 3).\n\nNote that the exact cooking time may vary depending on the size of the roast, so adjust the cooking time accordingly. Also, make sure to check the internal temperature of the meat to ensure that it is cooked all the way through.", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 26.273, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 127, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1191, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10224, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 18501, 11, 4296, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 11, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 50761, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 374, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 11, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13], "logp_list": [-0.7936, -0.0121, -0.0025, -0.0016, -0.0001, -0.0119, -0.0258, -0.0031, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0656, -0.5686, -0.0014, -0.0133, -0.002, -0.0, -0.0197, -0.0001, -0.0153, -0.0045, -0.1179, -0.0241, -0.0002, -0.0037, -0.0285, -0.0136, -0.2243, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.006, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0028, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0088, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.0009, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.9111, -0.0004, -0.0017, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0011, -0.0017, -0.0003, -0.0129, -0.0124, -0.0591, -0.0002, -0.0343, -0.0009, -0.0019, -0.0058, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.0042, -0.0019, -0.1218, -0.0029, -0.0003, -0.0005, -0.0007, -0.0909, -0.0341, -0.0028, -0.