{"id": "395", "pred": "We should want to serve God because we know Him; an inherent part of knowing Him is a desire to serve Him. It's always been God's intention to make us like His Son, Jesus", "raw_output": "We should want to serve God because we know Him; an inherent part of knowing Him is a desire to serve Him. It's always been God's intention to make us like His Son, Jesus", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"Why should we serve others?\"\n\nWe should serve others because it is a way to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who may not treat us well. Serving others is an expression of our love for God and our desire to be like Him. When we truly know God, our natural response is a desire to love and serve Him in return, and serving others is a way to do so. Additionally, serving others without self-serving motives and expecting nothing in return allows us to serve out of love and build stronger character muscles.\n\nTherefore, serving others is not only a way to show love and kindness, but it is also a way to deepen our relationship with God and grow in our faith.", "question": "why should we serve others", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 8.188, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 39, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1654, 1265, 1366, 311, 8683, 4264, 1576, 582, 1414, 20426, 26, 458, 36988, 949, 315, 14063, 20426, 374, 264, 12591, 311, 8683, 20426, 13, 1084, 594, 2677, 1012, 4264, 594, 14602, 311, 1281, 601, 1075, 5301, 11840, 11, 10588], "logp_list": [-0.76, -0.0933, -1.5158, -0.0006, -0.0028, -0.5797, -0.148, -0.0587, -0.0315, -0.0082, -0.3652, -0.0126, -0.0033, -0.0025, -0.0009, -0.0599, -0.0039, -0.0047, -0.0019, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0011, -0.0017, -0.0503, -0.5314, -0.1176, -0.0695, -0.002, -0.0006, -0.0014, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0002, -0.0006, -0.0017, -0.0016, -0.0083, -0.0016], "cumulative_logprob": -4.4437, "norm_logp": -0.1139, "input_len": 531, "output_tokens": 39, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 20.34, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "402", "pred": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin the hold the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "raw_output": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin the hold the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "gt": "To remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to remove the screws inside the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. There is also a pin on the outer edge of the door that needs to be removed. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off.", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 21.509, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 86, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 279, 14639, 6006, 6945, 304, 697, 57298, 472, 17088, 11, 498, 686, 1184, 311, 4057, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 315, 279, 6006, 6815, 323, 1052, 594, 1083, 825, 304, 279, 6149, 315, 279, 4766, 6006, 3705, 13, 1913, 279, 15955, 6821, 315, 279, 6006, 1052, 594, 1083, 264, 8983, 279, 3331, 279, 6945, 304, 1992, 11, 498, 686, 1184, 311, 4057, 429, 13, 5005, 990, 264, 6006, 6945, 16652, 5392, 311, 81279, 279, 6006, 6945, 1007, 315, 279, 472, 17088, 14639, 6006, 13], "logp_list": [-0.8951, -0.0085, -0.0037, -0.0574, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0302, -0.2324, -0.3569, -0.036, -0.0001, -0.0455, -0.0679, -0.009, -0.0009, -0.0009, -0.0277, -0.0351, -0.01, -0.0001, -0.0023, -0.0022, -0.0032, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0207, -1.2666, -0.0492, -0.0291, -0.0131, -0.0022, -0.0025, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.008, -0.0036, -0.2131, -0.2093, -0.0183, -0.0548, -0.0658, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.1617, -0.0066, -0.0014, -0.0012, -0.0006, -0.6877, -0.0578, -0.0012, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0003, -0.0265, -0.0074, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0025, -0.086, -0.0838, -0.0404, -0.0109, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0039, -0.0005, -0.0048, -0.0003, -0.0045, -0.0014, -0.0283], "cumulative_logprob": -5.0136, "norm_logp": -0.0583, "input_len": 512, "output_tokens": 86, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 71.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "406", "pred": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin the hold the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "raw_output": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin the hold the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n\nAfter removing the screws and clips, you will be able to remove the door panel. It is recommended to watch an instructional video to see the process and locate the parts mentioned.", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 21.299, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 86, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 279, 14639, 6006, 6945, 304, 697, 57298, 472, 17088, 11, 498, 686, 1184, 311, 4057, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 315, 279, 6006, 6815, 323, 1052, 594, 1083, 825, 304, 279, 6149, 315, 279, 4766, 6006, 3705, 13, 1913, 279, 15955, 6821, 315, 279, 6006, 1052, 594, 1083, 264, 8983, 279, 3331, 279, 6945, 304, 1992, 11, 498, 686, 1184, 311, 4057, 429, 13, 5005, 990, 264, 6006, 6945, 16652, 5392, 311, 81279, 279, 6006, 6945, 1007, 315, 279, 472, 17088, 14639, 6006, 13], "logp_list": [-0.8951, -0.0085, -0.0037, -0.0574, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0302, -0.2324, -0.3569, -0.036, -0.0001, -0.0455, -0.0679, -0.009, -0.0009, -0.0009, -0.0277, -0.0351, -0.01, -0.0001, -0.0023, -0.0022, -0.0032, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0207, -1.2666, -0.0492, -0.0291, -0.0131, -0.0022, -0.0025, -0.0005, -0.0005, -0.008, -0.0036, -0.2131, -0.2093, -0.0183, -0.0548, -0.0658, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0006, -0.0009, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.1617, -0.0066, -0.0014, -0.0012, -0.0006, -0.6877, -0.0578, -0.0012, -0.0003, -0.0008, -0.0003, -0.0265, -0.0074, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0025, -0.086, -0.0838, -0.0404, -0.0109, -0.0003, -0.0007, -0.0006, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0011, -0.0007, -0.0013, -0.0039, -0.0005, -0.0048, -0.0003, -0.0045, -0.0014, -0.0283], "cumulative_logprob": -5.0136, "norm_logp": -0.0583, "input_len": 512, "output_tokens": 86, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.58, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "411", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "raw_output": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nIf you want to store the panko crumbs for later use, you can transfer them to an airtight container and keep them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 22.135, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 100, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 13, 10771, 678, 315, 279, 139