{"id": "518", "pred": "The reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards. Your entry ticket has a number on it from 1 to approximately 55. Tickets are $50 each and a table consists of 20 individuals, which constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. and two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pull. individuals totaling twenty.", "raw_output": "The reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards. Your entry ticket has a number on it from 1 to approximately 55. Tickets are $50 each and a table consists of 20 individuals, which constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. and two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pull. individuals totaling twenty.", "gt": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have the opportunity to win prizes. The specific details and mechanics of a raffle can vary. In a reverse raffle, participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, and the last ticket drawn wins the main prize. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the proceeds go to the winner of a random draw, while the other 50% is allocated for a charitable purpose. In some cases, raffles may also offer additional opportunities to win prizes, such as cash tip board raffles.", "question": "how do raffles work", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 16.806, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 82, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 9931, 435, 44090, 374, 264, 435, 44090, 714, 28412, 13, 4615, 4343, 11727, 702, 264, 1372, 389, 432, 504, 220, 16, 311, 13187, 220, 20, 20, 13, 35615, 525, 400, 20, 15, 1817, 323, 264, 1965, 17167, 315, 220, 17, 15, 7775, 11, 892, 41575, 825, 4583, 11727, 518, 400, 16, 15, 15, 15, 13, 323, 1378, 400, 20, 15, 15, 37408, 320, 603, 369, 279, 4124, 11958, 13330, 323, 825, 369, 279, 1156, 11727, 6815, 13, 7775, 81123, 17073, 13], "logp_list": [