{"id": "651", "pred": "The color of urine can vary based on several factors, including the presence of blood, certain foods and medications, and kidney diseases. A normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this pale color of urine is sometimes altered when, in case of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunction function", "raw_output": "The color of urine can vary based on several factors, including the presence of blood, certain foods and medications, and kidney diseases. A normal color of urine is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this pale color of urine is sometimes altered when, in case of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunction function", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the color of urine can indicate various things, including:\n\n* Blood in the urine (passage 1)\n* Porphyria (a rare inherited disorder) (passage 2)\n* Kidney diseases (passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What does the color of urine mean?\" is:\n\nAnswer: Depending on the passage, the color of urine can indicate different things, such as blood, porphyria, or kidney diseases.", "question": "color of urin meaning", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 15.561, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 77, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 3118, 389, 3807, 9363, 11, 2670, 279, 9362, 315, 6543, 11, 3654, 15298, 323, 29910, 11, 323, 37942, 18808, 13, 362, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 419, 27539, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 7025, 28752, 979, 11, 304, 1142, 315, 37942, 18808, 11, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 525, 71187, 729], "logp_list": [-0.2917, -0.0261, -0.0022, -0.0233, -0.0528, -1.0328, -1.171, -0.0004, -0.6472, -0.0018, -0.886, -0.073, -0.5647, -0.0345, -0.0019, -0.1356, -0.266, -0.4401, -0.3125, -0.5159, -0.0035, -0.0171, -0.1814, -1.1767, -0.1835, -0.0602, -1.3676, -0.61, -0.5066, -0.5314, -0.0014, -0.0081, -0.0422, -0.0002, -0.5233, -0.7909, -0.0131, -0.019, -0.0001, -0.0098, -0.0003, -0.0038, -0.0, -0.0, -0.012, -0.1881, -0.0, -1.508, -0.1634, -0.0013, -0.0238, -0.0009, -0.1701, -0.0006, -0.0016, -0.0924, -0.106, -0.0008, -0.058, -0.0006, -0.0022, -0.0007, -0.0054, -0.0072, -0.0003, -0.0011, -0.0024, -0.0026, -0.0083, -0.0001, -0.0018, -0.0011, -0.0009, -0.0004, -0.1744, -0.0032, -0.5051], "cumulative_logprob": -15.5745, "norm_logp": -0.2023, "input_len": 243, "output_tokens": 77, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "656", "pred": "Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion.", "raw_output": "Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few mintues. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion.", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Rinse your hair completely with water.\n2. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n3. Apply a conditioner and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n4. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n5. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles.\n\nAdditionally, it is recommended to use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair after washing, and to be gentle when handling wet hair to prevent damage.", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 16.308, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 81, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [49, 258, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 323, 11, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 990, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 13, 26530, 279, 64324, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 28337, 1137, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 13], "logp_list": [-1.5496, -0.0021, -0.0001, -0.1992, -0.0003, -0.0561, -0.7533, -0.1297, -0.0266, -0.0038, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0026, -0.0007, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0044, -0.002, -0.0007, -0.0005, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0014, -0.001, -0.0004, -0.0571, -0.3346, -0.0083, -0.0003, -0.007, -0.0004, -0.0002, -0.0005, -0.0055, -0.2239, -0.0098, -0.0001, -0.0093, -0.0048, -0.001, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0209, -0.0019, -0.0004, -0.0008, -0.0007, -0.1846, -0.0009, -0.002, -0.0051, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0001, -0.0004, -0.0022, -0.0001, -0.0049, -0.0031, -0.0018, -0.0001, -0.0005, -0.0032, -0.0156, -0.0005, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0012, -0.0002, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0081], "cumulative_logprob": -3.6646, "norm_logp": -0.0452, "input_len": 406, "output_tokens": 81, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.21, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "663", "pred": "To use vinegar for dogs, you can mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse, spray vinegar full-strength on your dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin, make a rinse to improve your dog's skin and coat, clean out your dog's ears using ACv, spray your dog's coat to repel fleas, bathe in ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas, use a flea comb to remove the fleas, rinse your", "raw_output": "To use vinegar for dogs, you can mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse, spray vinegar full-strength on your dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin, make a rinse to improve your dog's skin and coat, clean out your dog's ears using ACv, spray your dog's coat to repel fleas, bathe in ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas, use a flea comb to remove the fleas, rinse your", "gt": "Sure, here are some possible answers based on the given passages:\n\nQ: What are some uses for vinegar when it comes to dogs?\n\nA: Vinegar can be used to:\n\n* Improve a dog's skin and coat by mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and using it as a final rinse.\n* Normalize the pH balance of a dog's skin by spraying full-strength vinegar on its coat.\n* Repel fleas by spraying a dog's coat with apple cider vinegar.\n* Soothe itchy ears by using a diluted solution of apple cider vinegar (50% water, 50% vinegar) on a cotton swab or gauze pad.\n* Clean a dog's ears by using apple cider vinegar.\n* Fight fleas by bathing a dog in a soap mixture that includes apple cider vinegar.\n* Remove fleas using a flea comb after bathing a dog in an apple cider vinegar soap mixture.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "opera", "has_visual": false, "n_image_tokens": 0, "time_sec": 21.193, "status": "success", "n_rollback": 0, "n_tokens": 106, "record_process": true, "token_